hadiths[289]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that while we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: “A man from among the people of Paradise will come to you now.” He said that a man from the Ansar came, water from ablution dripping from his beard, holding his shoes in his left hand. When the next day came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A man from among the people of Paradise will come to you now.” The same man came, and he was in the same state as before. When the next day came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A man from among the people of Paradise will come to you now.” The same man came, and he was in the same state as before. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and left, Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) followed him and said to him: I had a dispute with my father and swore that I would not stay with him for three nights. If you can host me for the sake of fulfilling my oath, then please do so. He said: All right. Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say: I stayed with that man for three nights. He did not stand for prayer at night, but whenever he turned on his bed, he would remember Allah and say «اللہ أکبر» , until he got up for the Fajr prayer and performed a complete ablution. Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Moreover, I only heard him speak good words. So when three nights had passed, I was close to considering his deeds insignificant. I said: O servant of Allah! The truth is that there was no anger or resentment between me and my father, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say three times in three gatherings: “A man from among the people of Paradise will come to you now.” And each time, it was you who came. I wanted to stay with you and observe your actions, then adopt them, but I did not see you doing any great deed. So what is it that has brought you to the rank that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned? He said: It is only what you have seen. I left from there, but as I turned away, he called me back and said: It is only what you have seen, except that I never hold any grudge in my heart against any Muslim, nor do I envy anyone for the good that Allah Almighty has granted him. Upon this, Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: This is the deed that has brought you to this rank, and we do not have the strength to do it."
"2","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) mentioned a man before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said that (no one) eats until he eats, and he does not depart until travel is made for him. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have backbitten him."" They said: ""We only mentioned (the fault) that was in him."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you have mentioned that (fault) which is in your brother, then that is sufficient to make you (sinful)."""
"3","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a Muslim visits his brother who is ill or meets him, Allah says: Your heart has become good, your walking has become good, and He has provided for you a place in Paradise as a house."""
"4","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that indeed a man set out to visit a brother of his in another town, so Allah appointed an angel on his path. When he reached him, the angel said, ""Where are you intending to go?"" He replied, ""I intend to visit a brother of mine in this town."" The angel said, ""Has he done any favor to you for which you are going to repay him?"" He said, ""No, I only love him for the sake of Allah."" The angel said, ""Indeed, I have been sent to you by Allah with this message: Surely, Allah also loves you as you love him for His sake."""
"5","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty will say on the Day of Resurrection, 'Where are those who loved one another for My Majesty? Today I will shelter them in My shade, on the day when there is no shade except My shade.'"""
"6","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, ""When any one of you loves his companion, he should go to him, to his house, and inform him that indeed he loves him for the sake of Allah. So I (Abu Salim Jaishani) have come to you (Abu Umayyah) in your house for this very reason."""
"7","Sayyiduna Abu Malik Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that indeed, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) completed his prayer, he turned his face towards the people and said: ""O people! Listen, understand, and know that surely there are some servants of Allah who are neither prophets nor martyrs, (but) the prophets and martyrs will envy them because of their gatherings and their closeness to Allah."" So, a man from among the distant Bedouins sat on his knees and, pointing towards the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with his hand, said: O Messenger of Allah! Are there some people among mankind who are neither prophets nor martyrs, (but) the prophets and martyrs will envy them because of their gatherings and their closeness to Allah? Please describe their qualities to us and portray them for us. At the question of this Bedouin, the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) became cheerful, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They are unknown people, belonging to foreign tribes, their mutual acquaintance is not due to close kinship, they loved each other for the sake of Allah and united upon that. Allah Almighty will make pulpits of light for them on the Day of Resurrection, then He will seat them upon them, their faces will be radiant and their garments will also be radiant. People will be in fear on the Day of Resurrection, but they will not be afraid, and they are the friends of Allah, upon whom there will be no fear, nor will they grieve."""
"8","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that indeed he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Surely, those people who love each other for the majesty of Allah will be under the shade of Allah's Throne, on the day when there will be no shade except His shade."""
"9","Sharjeel bin Simt said to Amr bin Abasah Salmi (may Allah be pleased with him): O son of Abasah! Will you narrate to me a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in which there is no addition, no falsehood, and not narrated from anyone except you who heard it from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)? He said: Yes. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Verily, Allah the Exalted says: ""Indeed, I have made My love obligatory for those who unite with each other for My sake. Indeed, I have made My love obligatory for those who mix with each other for My sake. Indeed, I have made My love obligatory for those who spend on each other for My sake. Indeed, I have made My love obligatory for those who help each other for My sake."""
"10","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Indeed, I have two neighbors; to which of them should I give a gift? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To the one whose door is closer to you."""
"11","Abdullah bin Samit narrates that indeed Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! A person acts for the sake of Allah, and people love him for it? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the hastened glad tidings for the believer."""
"12","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) used to like it when people from the villages would come and ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) questions. So, a Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! When will the Hour (Day of Judgment) come?” The call for the prayer was given. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and led the prayer. Then, when he finished his prayer, he said: “Where is the one who asked about the Hour?” He said: “I am here, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)!” He further said: “I have not prepared for it many prayers or fasts, but indeed I love Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him).” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A person will be with those whom he loves.” He said: I have not seen the Muslims as happy about anything after accepting Islam as they were about this statement."
"13","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whenever two people love each other in Islam, and then discord is created between them, it is necessarily due to a sin committed by one of them."""
"14","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: O people! Show mercy to one another, for indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say with my own ears: “The Muslims are like a single person; when any of his limbs is afflicted, the rest of his body feels the pain.”"
"15","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no sin more deserving that its perpetrator be punished swiftly in this world, along with what is stored for him in the Hereafter, than oppression, rebellion, and severing of ties."""
"16","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man entered Paradise because of a branch of a thorny tree that was in the path of the Muslims, which he removed from the way."""
"17","Bahz narrates from his father Hakim, and he from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Woe to the person who speaks and lies in order to make people laugh with it; woe to him, woe to him.”"
"18","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a servant utters a word, he speaks it only to make people laugh, but because of it he falls farther (into Hell) than the distance between the heaven and the earth, and indeed, he slips with his tongue more severely than he slips with his feet."""
"19","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is sufficient for a man to be considered sinful that he relates everything he hears."""
"20","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the first and the last (of people) will be gathered, it will be said: This is the deception of so-and-so, son of so-and-so."""
"21","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I imitated a woman or a man in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not like to imitate anyone, and even if I were to have such and such, it would be considered very great."""
"22","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Bahili (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) had his new shirt brought and wore it. I do not think it even reached his collarbones, until he (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “All praise is due to Allah who has clothed me with (this garment) with which I cover my private parts and with which I adorn myself in my life.” Then he said: “Do you know why I said this? I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace and blessings be upon him) had his new clothes brought, wore them—I think they reached his collarbones—until he (peace and blessings be upon him) said the like of what I said. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘By the One in whose hand is my soul! Whenever a Muslim servant wears new clothes and then says the like of what I have said, then he turns to his old and worn-out clothes which he has taken off and gives them to a Muslim, poor, or needy person, and he gives them only for the sake of Allah, then surely he is in Allah’s protection, guarantee, and neighborhood, as long as even a single thread of it remains upon him, whether he is alive or dead, alive or dead, alive or dead.’”"
"23","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said one day while we were with him: “Glad tidings for the strangers, glad tidings for the strangers!” It was asked, “Who are the strangers, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “A few righteous people who will be among many evil people; those who disobey will be more than those who obey among them.” And one day they were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when the sun rose, he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Soon, on the Day of Resurrection, some people from my Ummah will come, their light will be like the light of the sun.” We asked, “Who are those people, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The poor emigrants, through whom people are protected from disliked things; if any one of them dies in such a state that his need remains in his heart, they will be gathered from the corners of the earth.”"
"24","Sayyiduna Hisham bin ‘Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: “It is not permissible for a Muslim to abandon another Muslim out of anger for more than three nights. As long as both of them persist in breaking off relations, they will be deviating from the truth, and the one who returns first—his initiative in returning will be an expiation for his (sins). And if he seeks reconciliation but the other does not accept, and he gives him salam, then the angels respond to him and Satan responds to the other. And if both of them die while persisting in this estrangement, neither of them will enter Paradise.” I think the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Ever.”"
"25","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl Sa‘idi (may Allah be pleased with him) that while we were reciting (the Qur’an), suddenly the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us and he said: “All praise is due to Allah, the Book is one and among you are the red and the black. Recite (the Qur’an) before there come people who will recite it, straighten its letters as an arrow is straightened, but it will not go beyond their collarbones. They will seek its reward quickly and will not delay in it.”"
"26","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from the people, but He takes away knowledge by taking away the scholars, until when He leaves no scholar, the people will take ignorant ones as leaders; they will be asked questions and will give verdicts without knowledge, they will go astray and will lead others astray."""
"27","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I saw some men whose lips were being cut with scissors. I asked: O Jibreel (peace be upon him)! Who are these? He said: They are the preachers of your ummah who enjoin good upon the people but forget their own selves, and they recite the Book. Do they then not understand?"""
"28","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), ""What is sin?"" He (peace be upon him) replied: ""Leave that which causes uneasiness in your chest."" The man asked, ""What is faith?"" He (peace be upon him) replied: ""When your sin displeases you and your good deed pleases you, then you are a believer."""
"29","Sayyiduna Fadala bin Ubaid (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said at the occasion of the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Shall I not inform you about the believer? He is the one from whom people are safe regarding their wealth and lives. And the Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand people are safe. And the Mujahid is the one who strives against his own self in obedience to Allah. And the emigrant is the one who abandons sins and mistakes.”"
"30","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who reports from the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: “Whoever possesses three qualities will taste the sweetness of faith: that he loves someone and loves him only for the sake of Allah; that Allah and His Messenger, peace and blessings be upon him, are more beloved to him than anything else; and that he would rather be thrown into the fire than return to disbelief after Allah has saved him from it.”"
"31","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I have not seen anything more beautiful than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), as if the sun was moving in his (peace be upon him) face. And I have not seen anyone who walked faster than the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), as if the earth was folded up for him (peace and blessings be upon him). Indeed, we would become tired, but he (peace and blessings be upon him) would feel no difficulty at all."
"32","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sa'di (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Has it not been reported to me that you (as a governor) perform many tasks for the people, and then when you are given wages, you do not accept them?"" He said, ""Yes."" Umar asked, ""What is your intention in this?"" He replied, ""I am wealthy, I have horses and many slaves, and I intend that my work be charity for the Muslims."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Do not do so. Indeed, I used to do the same as you are doing, but when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave me wages, I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, give this to someone who is more in need of it than me.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Take it, either make it your wealth or give it in charity. And whatever comes to you from this wealth, and you are neither greedy for it nor asking for it, then take it. And whatever is not like that, do not let your soul pursue it.'"""
"33","Qais bin Bishr Taghlabi said that my father was a companion of Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) in Damascus, and there was a man among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in Damascus, who was called Ibn Hanzalah (may Allah have mercy on him). He was inclined to solitude and would rarely sit in gatherings with people. He would only be engaged in prayer, and when he finished the prayer, his only occupation was to say Subhan Allah, Alhamdulillah, and Allahu Akbar, until he reached his family. One day he passed by us while we were with Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him). He greeted us with salam, so Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: Tell us something that will benefit us and not harm you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to us: ""Indeed, you are going to your brothers, so keep your clothes tidy and keep your mounts tidy, so that you become prominent among the people. Indeed, Allah does not like indecency or deliberate obscenity."""
"34","Aseer bin Jaber said that we used to sit with one of our hadith scholars in Kufa. When people dispersed, a few men would remain, among them was a man who would not listen to anyone, he would only speak his own words, so I liked him and his love became rooted in my heart. I was like this when suddenly I found him missing, so I asked my companions: There was a man who used to sit with us, does anyone among you know him? They said: Yes, he is Owais Qarni. I said: Can you tell me where his house is? They said: Yes. I went with him until we reached his room and knocked on the door. He came out, so I said: O brother! What has prevented you from coming to us? He said: Nakedness, I have nothing (no clothing) in which I can come to you, I have only one sheet. I said: Then wear this sheet. He said: Do not do so, indeed if I wear this sheet, they will harm me. So I kept insisting with him until he wore it. He came out to them, so they said: Has he deceived someone with his sheet? He came and took it off. I came to them and said: What do you intend towards this man, surely you have harmed him, he wears clothes once and takes them off the next time? I rebuked them harshly with my tongue. Among his companions was a man who used to mock him. The delegation of the people of Kufa came to Sayyidina Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and that man also came with the delegation. Sayyidina Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: Is there anyone here from the people of Qarn? That man came forward. Sayyidina Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The matter is that a man from the people of Yemen will come to you who will be called Owais Qarni, he will leave no one in Yemen except his mother, he will have leprosy, he will pray to Allah, and Allah will remove it from him except for a spot the size of a dinar or dirham. Whoever among you meets him, let him request him to seek forgiveness for him."" (Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said:) He came to us here, I said: Who are you? He said: Owais. I said: Whom did you leave behind in Yemen? He said: My mother. I said: Did you have leprosy, and you prayed to Allah and He removed it from you except for a spot the size of a dinar or dirham? He said: Yes. I said: Pray for forgiveness for me. He said: O Commander of the Faithful! Should someone like me pray for forgiveness for someone like you? I said: You are my brother, you cannot be separated from me. He quickly left me, and I was informed that he came to you in Kufa. That man began to belittle what Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) had said about him and said: That person is not from among us, nor do we know him. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Why not, indeed he is such and such a man, and he began to describe his qualities. He said: That man is among us, he is mocked, he is called Owais. He said: That is him, you have found him, and I did not think you would be able to find him. That man came and before going home, he came to him. Owais said: This is not your habit, what has appeared to you? He said: I swear by Allah! I met Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and he said such and such things, pray for forgiveness for me. He said: I will never pray for forgiveness for you until you make it obligatory upon yourself that you will not mock me, and you will not mention to anyone what you heard from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: This is my promise to you. He prayed for forgiveness for him. Aseer said: Only a little time had passed when his story spread in Kufa. I stayed with him and said: O my brother! I do not think that you are afflicted with self-admiration, and we absolutely did not care about it. He said: There is nothing in it that I should go around telling people, every servant will only get the reward of his deeds. When the matter spread, he ran away and left."
"35","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, Allah has one hundred mercies. Out of them, He has sent down one mercy among the jinn, humans, cattle, and insects, so that they show compassion and kindness to one another, and because of it, wild animals show affection to their young. And the remaining ninety-nine mercies, He will show mercy to His servants with them on the Day of Resurrection."""
"36","Dhamdham bin Hawas said: I entered the mosque of Madinah when an elderly man called out to me and said: O Yamami! O Yamami! Come here, and I did not recognize him. He said: Never say to any man: Allah will never forgive you, nor will He admit you to Paradise. I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him). I said: These words, when one of us is angry, he says to some of his family, or his wife, or his servant. He said: Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Indeed, among the Children of Israel there were two men who loved each other. One of them strove in worship, and the other— as if the Prophet (peace be upon him) was saying— was a sinner. So the worshipper would say: Refrain from the state you are in, stop! He would say: Leave me and my Lord, until one day he found him involved in a sin, so he disliked it and said: Stop! He said: Leave me and my Lord, have you been sent as a guardian over me? He said: By Allah! Allah will never forgive you, nor will He ever admit you to Paradise! He (the Prophet) said: Allah Almighty sent an angel to both of them, who took their souls, and they both stood before Allah. Allah said to the sinner: Enter Paradise by My mercy, and to the other He said: Do you have power to withhold My mercy from My servant? He said: No, O Lord! He said: Take him to the Fire.” Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By Him in Whose hand is my soul! Indeed, he uttered a word that destroyed his world and his Hereafter."
"37","Humran, who was the freed slave of Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), narrates that a water jug passed by Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). He (may Allah be pleased with him) called for it, performed ablution, and completed his ablution thoroughly. Then he said, ""If I had heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) only once, twice, or three times, I would certainly not have narrated it to you. I have heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say (countless times): 'Whoever performs ablution and completes his ablution well, then stands for prayer, Allah will surely forgive his sins that are between that prayer and the next prayer.'"" Ka'b bin Muhammad said, ""Whenever I heard a hadith from any companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), I would search for it in the Qur'an. So I searched for it and found it: « إِنَّا فَتَحْنَا لَكَ فَتْحًا مُبِينًا (١) لِيَغْفِرَ لَكَ اللَّهُ مَا تَقَدَّمَ مِنْ ذَنْبِكَ وَمَا تَأَخَّرَ وَيُتِمَّ نِعْمَتَهُ عَلَيْكَ » (Al-Fath: 1,2) 'Indeed, We have given you a clear conquest, that Allah may forgive for you what preceded of your sin and what will follow and complete His favor upon you.' So I realized that indeed Allah did not complete His favor upon him (peace and blessings be upon him) until He forgave his sin. Then I recited this verse: « إِذَا قُمْتُمْ إِلَى الصَّلَاةِ فَاغْسِلُوا وُجُوهَكُمْ وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ إِلَى الْمَرَافِقِ » (Al-Ma'idah: 6) 'When you rise for prayer, wash your faces and your hands up to the elbows.' Until I reached: « وَلَكِنْ يُرِيدُ لِيُطَهِّرَكُمْ وَلِيُتِمَّ نِعْمَتَهُ عَلَيْكُمْ » (Al-Ma'idah: 6) 'But He wants to purify you and complete His favor upon you.' So I recognized that indeed Allah did not complete His favor upon them until He forgave them."""
"38","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Prayers are an expiation for sins, prayers are an expiation for sins, and if you wish, recite: « إِنَّ الْحَسَنَاتِ يُذْهِبْنَ السَّيِّئَاتِ ذَلِكَ ذِكْرَى لِلذَّاكِرِينَ » (Hud: 114) 'Indeed, good deeds erase bad deeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.'"""
"39","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Wathilah bin Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Allah says: I am as My servant thinks of Me, so let him think of Me as he wishes.”"
"40","Sa’sa’ah bin Mu’awiyah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that I met Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him). He asked: ""Where are you from?"" I said: ""From the people of Iraq."" He said: ""Shall I not narrate to you a hadith that will benefit those who come after you as well?"" I said: ""Why not?"" He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Indeed, the first thing for which people will be called to account on the Day of Resurrection is the prayer. Allah will say to the angels: Look at My servant’s prayer. If it is complete, it will be recorded as complete, and if it is deficient, Allah the Exalted, in His forbearance and grace, will say: Return it to My servant; see if he has any voluntary prayers. If he has any voluntary prayers, his obligatory prayer will be completed with them.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Then the rest of the deeds will be taken in the same manner.'"""
"41","Sayyiduna Abu Amrah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that during a military expedition we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and the people were afflicted with hunger. The people sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to slaughter some of the riding animals and said, “Surely, through them Allah will cause us to reach (our destination).” When Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) saw that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to grant them permission, he said, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What will be our condition when we meet the people naked, hungry, and on foot? But O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! If you deem it appropriate, call the people with their remaining provisions, gather them, then supplicate to Allah for blessing in it. Surely, Allah will cause us to reach (our destination) due to your supplication, or he said: Soon, due to your supplication, blessing will be placed for us?” Thus, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called the people with their remaining provisions. The people began to bring a handful of grain and more than that, and the one who brought the most brought a sa’ (about 2100 grams) of dates. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gathered them, then stood up and supplicated for whatever Allah willed him to ask. Then he called the army with their vessels and commanded them to fill them up by scooping (from the provisions). There was not a single vessel in the army except that it was filled, and the provisions were still left. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled until his molar teeth became visible. He said, “I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, and I bear witness that indeed I am the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Whoever among the believing servants meets Allah with these two (testimonies), they will become a barrier for him against the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"42","Sayyiduna Rifa’ah Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), until when we were at the place of al-Kudair or Qudayd, some of us began to seek permission to go to their families, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) granted them permission. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) praised Allah and said: “Seek goodness.” Then he said: “I bear witness before Allah that any servant who dies, bearing witness that there is no deity except Allah and indeed Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger, with sincerity of heart, and then remains steadfast, then surely Allah will admit him into Paradise. And indeed, my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, has promised me that He will admit seventy thousand from my Ummah into Paradise without any reckoning and without any punishment. And indeed, I firmly hope that before their entry, you and your righteous wives and children will have already taken your places in the homes of Paradise.” And he said: “When half the night or a third of the night passes, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, descends to the lowest heaven and says: ‘None of My servants can ask except from Me. Who is there who seeks forgiveness from Me so that I may forgive him? Who is there who supplicates to Me so that I may answer his supplication? Who is there who asks of Me so that I may give him?’—until the dawn breaks.”"
"43","Sayyiduna Mahmood bin Rabee’ (may Allah be pleased with him) thought that he understood from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and it was the mouthful of water which the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) spat from the bucket at his house. He said: I heard Sayyiduna ‘Itbaan bin Malik Al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him), who was one of the Banu Salim, saying: I used to lead my people, Banu Salim, in prayer. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: Indeed, my eyesight has gone, and floods come between me and my people, so I wish that you, O Messenger of Allah, would come and pray at a place in my house, so that I may take it as a mosque. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I will do so, insha’Allah.” So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came in the morning when the sun had risen high, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was with him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sought permission, and I gave him permission. He did not sit until he said: Where would you like me to pray in your house? I pointed to a place where I liked him to pray. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up, and we formed rows behind him. Then he finished the prayer with salam, and we also finished with salam. When he had finished, we detained him for some khazeer (a dish made of meat and flour) which had been prepared. The people of the neighborhood heard about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and they began to announce hospitality in their neighborhoods, so they gathered until the house was filled to capacity. A man said: Where is Malik bin Dukhshun? Another man said: He is a hypocrite, he does not love Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do not say that about him. He says la ilaha illallah, seeking only the Face of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.” He said: But we see his inclination and conversation with the hypocrites. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do not say that about him. He says la ilaha illallah, seeking only the Face of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. They said: Why not, O Messenger of Allah! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever comes on the Day of Resurrection saying la ilaha illallah, seeking by it the Face of Allah, Allah will certainly make the Fire forbidden for him.” Mahmood (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I narrated this hadith to some people among whom was Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him), the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), in the campaign in which he died with Yazid bin Mu’awiyah. He rejected it from me and said: I do not think that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) definitely said what you have narrated. This was hard on me, so I said: For Allah’s sake, I vow that if He returns me safely from the campaign, I will ask ‘Itbaan bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) about it. So I found him alive, and I entered ihram for Hajj or ‘Umrah from Ilya, until I came to Madinah and went to Banu Salim, where ‘Itbaan bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) was, very old, his eyesight gone, and he was the imam of his people. When he finished his prayer with salam, I came and greeted him and told him who I was, and he narrated to me this hadith just as he had narrated it to me the first time. Zuhri said: But it is not known whether this was before the obligations of the Qur’an were revealed, for Allah the Exalted has made many obligations in His Book upon those who say this word, which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned. We fear that the matter has shifted to those who are able not to be deceived, so he should not be deceived."
"44","The companion of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Busr (may Allah be pleased with him), narrates that a man said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Which deed is the most virtuous? He (peace be upon him) replied: “Let your tongue always remain moist with the remembrance of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic.”"
"45","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrate from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “Whenever people gather together to remember Allah, the angels surely surround them, tranquility descends upon them, mercy envelops them, and Allah mentions them among those who are with Him.” That is, the angels."
"46","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever says something to make his companions laugh, because of that he falls (into Hell) farther than Thurayya (the Pleiades)."""
"47","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whenever people sit in a gathering and do not remember Allah in it, then surely that gathering will be a source of regret and remorse for them. And whoever walks even a little and neither remembers Allah nor sends blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), then this (walking) too will certainly be a cause of regret and remorse for him.”"
"48","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever people sit in a gathering in which they neither remember Allah nor send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that (gathering) will surely be a cause of regret and remorse for them on the Day of Resurrection. If He wills, He may forgive them, and if He wills, He may punish them because of it."""
"49","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to deliver the sermon on Friday while leaning against a wooden trunk with his back. When the people increased in number, he (peace be upon him) said: “Make a pulpit for me.” So the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) made a pulpit for him (peace be upon him). It was merely a time of hardship, so he (peace be upon him) moved from the wood to the pulpit. He said: “Then it (the trunk) began to weep. By Allah! That wood wept like a father weeps.” Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: And by Allah! I was in the mosque, hearing its (weeping). He said: By Allah! It continued to weep until the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) descended from the pulpit, went towards it, embraced it to his chest, and then it became silent, and there was longing in it. (Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him) said: O assembly of Muslims! The wooden trunk is weeping for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so are not those who hope to meet him (peace be upon him) more deserving of longing towards him?"
"50","Sayyiduna Amir bin Rabi’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever sends blessings upon me, the angels seek forgiveness for him as long as he continues to send blessings. So let a servant do it less or more.”"
"51","Sayyiduna Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came one day, and happiness was apparent on his face. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The matter is that Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to me and said: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon you)! Are you not pleased that for whoever from your Ummah sends blessings upon you once, I will send ten mercies upon him, and whoever sends peace upon you once, I will send ten salutations upon him?”"
"52","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there are some angels of Allah who travel about on the earth; they convey to me the greetings (salam) of my ummah."""
"53","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir al-Juhani رضي الله عنه narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم say: “Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then offers a prayer in which he neither forgets nor plays, then whatever (mistake) he committed before it, it will erase it.”"
"54","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer is in sets of two rak‘ahs. In every two rak‘ahs there is tashahhud (at-tahiyyat), and one should adopt humility, submissiveness, and meekness. Then you should raise your two hands,"" the narrator says: raise them towards your Lord, with the inner sides facing your face, ""O my Lord! Whoever does not do so, his prayer is incomplete."""
"55","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any one of you stands in prayer, indeed mercy is before him, so he should absolutely not move the pebbles."""
"56","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah remains attentive to His servant as long as he does not turn away (with distraction) in prayer. But when he turns his face away, He also turns away from him."""
"57","Ya’la bin Mamlak (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that indeed he asked Sayyida Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) about the recitation and prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). She said: What is your connection with the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)? He (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray, then sleep for as long as he had prayed, then pray for as long as he had slept, then sleep for as long as he had prayed. Thus, this was his (peace and blessings be upon him) prayer until morning came. And she described his (peace and blessings be upon him) recitation, suddenly she was describing his recitation letter by letter, making each letter clear and distinct."
"58","Muslim bin Mukhrāq said: I said to Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), ""O Mother of the Believers! Indeed, there are some people among whom one of them recites the entire Qur'an two or three times in one night."" She replied, ""They have recited, but they have not recited. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would stand in prayer for the entire night; he would recite Surah Al-Baqarah, Surah Aal-e-Imran, and Surah An-Nisa. Then, whenever he passed by a verse of glad tidings, he would certainly supplicate and show eagerness, and whenever he passed by a verse of warning, he would certainly supplicate to Allah Almighty and seek refuge."""
"59","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Envy is permissible only towards two men: one whom Allah has granted wealth and he spends from it during the hours of the day, and the other whom He has given this Qur'an, and he stands with it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day."""
"60","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Envy is only (allowed) towards two persons: one is the man whom Allah has given wealth and granted him the ability to spend it in the right way, and the other is the man whom Allah has granted wisdom, so he judges with it and teaches it (to others).”"
"61","Sa’ib bin Yazid narrated that indeed Shurayh Hadrami was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so he (peace be upon him) said: “He is a man who does not use the Qur’an as a pillow.”"
"62","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is an hour during the night, if any Muslim servant attains it while asking for goodness and virtue, it is certainly granted to him, and that (hour) is in every night."""
"63","Abu Muslim said that I asked Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Which part of the night is the best for standing (in prayer)?"" Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I also asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) just as you have asked me, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'The middle of the night.'"" 'Awf (the narrator) is in doubt, and those who do it are few."
"64","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I did not consider it difficult for my ummah, I would have certainly ordered them to use the miswak at every ablution, and to delay the ‘Isha prayer until midnight or one-third of the night. The matter is that when half the night or one-third of the night passes,"" then (the Prophet, peace be upon him) mentioned the descent of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, (and said that) He says: ""Who is there to call upon Me so that I may answer his prayer? Who is there to ask of Me so that I may grant him? Who is there to seek forgiveness from Me so that I may forgive him, until the sun rises."""
"65","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever spends the night in a state of ablution, an angel spends the night in the garment that touches his body. Whenever he wakes up during the night, the angel says: O Allah! Forgive Your such-and-such servant, for indeed he spent the night in a state of ablution."""
"66","Sulaiman Taimi, may Allah have mercy on him, said that a man narrated that it was said to the slave of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, Ubaid: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, command any prayer besides the obligatory prayers? He said: Yes, between Maghrib and Isha."
"67","Shuraih bin Hani (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I asked Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). She replied: Of all the prayers, there was none more deserving to be delayed than the 'Isha prayer, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was engaged in conversation. Whenever he (peace and blessings be upon him) performed this ('Isha) prayer and then came to me, he would certainly pray four or six rak'ahs. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) never protected himself from the ground with anything, except that I certainly remember a rainy day, when we spread a mat or something else under him, as the narrator mentioned, i.e., a leather mat, as if I am seeing the hole in it from which water was coming out."
"68","Sayyiduna Saeed bin Mundhir Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that he said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Can I recite the Qur'an in three nights? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you have the strength (then recite it)."" He said that he used to recite it like this until he passed away."
"69","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said that whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) left from my place, he would definitely perform two rak'ahs (units of prayer)."
"70","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any one of you enters the mosque, he should perform two rak‘ahs before sitting down."""
"71","Imam Abdullah bin Mubarak (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated a similar hadith with this chain from Malik bin Anas (may Allah have mercy on him) (as has been mentioned above)."
"72","Katheer A‘raj said: We were at “Dhi Sawari” (a place), and with us was Abu Fatimah Azdi, whose forehead and knees had become blackened due to the abundance of prostrations. (He narrated: I said, O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Tell me of a deed upon which I may remain steadfast and perform it. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Adopt prostrations abundantly, for indeed, whenever you perform a single prostration for Allah, Allah will raise you one degree in rank and will forgive you one sin because of it.”)"
"73","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ayub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed (with them) for a month. I remained for all the tasks of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). I saw that when the sun would decline or incline, or as I have said, if the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was engaged in any worldly matter, he would leave it, and if he was asleep, it was as if we would wake him up for it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would stand, perform ghusl or ablution, then he would pray four rak‘ahs, complete them, beautify them, and perform them with great calmness and composure. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to leave (our house), I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! You stayed with me for a month, and indeed I have come to know that surely you are filled with goodness and virtue from this. I remained with you to know all your actions (to closely observe the prescribed acts), I saw that when the sun would decline or incline, if there was any task in your hand, you would leave it, if you were asleep, you would be awakened, you would perform ghusl or ablution, then pray four rak‘ahs, you would complete them, beautify them, and perform them with great calmness and composure. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, the gates of the heavens and the gates of Paradise are opened at that hour for it. Whoever performs this prayer, then I have preferred that at that hour, goodness and virtue ascend for me to my Lord.”"
"74","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with them both), who reports from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that indeed supplication is worship. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited (the verse): ﴿وَقَالَ رَبُّكُمُ ادْعُونِي أَسْتَجِبْ لَكُمْ﴾ (Al-Mu’min: 60) “And your Lord said: Call upon Me; I will respond to you.”"
"75","The same hadith has been narrated through another chain of transmission."
"76","Abu Bakr bin Abdur Rahman bin Harith bin Hisham narrates that indeed Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with them both) entered the mosque and performed two light rak‘ahs. A man said to him: O Abu Yaqzan! Surely I have memorized them. He replied: Did you see me omit anything from their prescribed limits? Rather, I shortened them; I hastened in them due to forgetfulness. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, a man certainly performs prayer, and perhaps nothing of his prayer is recorded for him except a tenth, a ninth, an eighth, a seventh, or a fifth of it."""
"77","Ma’dan bin Abi Talhah Yamari said that Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me: Where is your residence? I said: In a village before Homs. Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whenever three people reside in a village or in the countryside and prayer is not established among them, then surely Satan overcomes them. So adhere to the congregation, for indeed the wolf eats the sheep that strays far.” Sa’ib (bin Hubaysh) said: By congregation, he meant the congregation of prayer."
"78","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever does not give up lying and acting upon it, and ignorance, then Allah has no need for him to give up his food and drink."""
"79","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “There are many who fast but gain nothing from their fast except hunger, and there are many who stand (in prayer at night) but gain nothing from their standing except wakefulness.”"
"80","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever spends two pairs (of something) in the way of Allah, he will be called from the gates of Paradise: O servant of Allah! This is better. If he is among those who pray, he will be called from the gate of prayer; if he is among those who give zakat, he will be called from the gate of zakat; if he is among those who strive (in jihad), he will be called from the gate of jihad; and if he is among those who fast, he will be called from the gate of Rayyan (the gate of abundant drink).” Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! May my parents be sacrificed for you, is there any need for someone to be called from all these gates (but) is there anyone who will be called from all these gates? He said: Yes, and I hope that you will be among them."
"81","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the most beloved deeds to Allah are those which are done consistently, even if they are few."" And whenever Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) performed any deed, she would adhere to it consistently."
"82","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Glad tidings for the person whose life is prolonged and whose deeds are good."""
"83","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ubaid bin Khalid Salmi (may Allah be pleased with him), and he is among the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), that (the Prophet, peace be upon him) established brotherhood between two men. One of them was martyred and the other died afterwards. We performed his funeral prayer, so the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""What did you say?"" They said: We prayed for him: O Allah! Have mercy on him, O Allah, unite him with his companion! So the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Then where did his prayer go after his companion's prayer? And where did his deeds go?"" And I think the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Where did his fasting go after his companion's fasting? The distance between the two is as much as the distance between the sky and the earth."" Amr bin Maymoon said that I like this hadith because he has narrated it to me with a chain of transmission."
"84","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “There are seven people whom Allah will grant shade under His (Throne’s) shade on the Day of Resurrection, the day when there will be no shade except His shade: a just ruler; and a youth who grew up in the worship of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic; and a man who remembered Allah in solitude and his eyes overflowed with tears; and a man whose heart is attached to the mosque; and two men who loved each other for the sake of Allah; and a man whom a woman of status and beauty called towards herself but he said, ‘Indeed, I fear Allah’; and a man who gave charity and concealed it so much that his left hand does not know what his right hand has given.”"
"85","Sha’bi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I heard Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with both of them) saying from the pulpit: “Restrain your fools, for indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Some people boarded a ship at sea, they divided their portions among themselves, and each man reached his allotted place. One of them took an axe and began to make a hole in his place. They said to him: What are you doing? He replied: This is my place, I will do in it as I wish. If they restrain his hands, they will be saved and he too will be saved, but if they leave him, he will drown and they too will drown. Therefore, restrain your fools before you are destroyed.”"
"86","Adi bin Adi Kindi narrates that one of our freed slaves told us that he heard my grandfather say that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""Indeed, Allah does not punish the common people because of the (evil deeds of) the elite, until they see evil among themselves and have the power to stop it, but do not stop it. When they do so, Allah afflicts the common people with punishment because of the elite."""
"87","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the mosque and saw two gatherings. One group was supplicating to Allah and turning towards Him with desire, and the other was learning and understanding the religion. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Both gatherings are upon goodness, but one is more virtuous than the other. As for these people, they are supplicating to Allah and turning towards Him; if He wills, He will grant them, and if He wills, He will not grant them. But these people are learning and teaching the ignorant, and I have only been sent as a teacher, so these people are superior.” Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) sat with them."
"88","Alqamah bin Waqas narrates that indeed Sayyiduna Bilal bin Harith Muzani (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: Certainly, I see you entering upon these rulers and covering them, so see with what you present yourself before them. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Surely a man utters a word of goodness, the end of which he does not realize, and because of it Allah writes for him His pleasure until the day he meets Him. And surely a man utters an evil word, the end of which he does not realize, and because of it Allah writes for him His displeasure until the day he meets Him."" Alqamah used to say that many a hadith which I heard from Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) became a barrier between me and him."
"89","Sayyidah Umm ‘Ammarah bint Ka‘b (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to my house, and I presented food before him. He (peace be upon him) said to me: “Eat.” I said that I am fasting. He (peace be upon him) said: “Indeed, when food is eaten in the presence of a fasting person, the angels pray for mercy and forgiveness for him, until they finish (eating).” Or he said: “Until they finish their food.”"
"90","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""If any one of you wishes to recognize the value of Allah's blessing upon him, then he should look at the one who is below him and not look at the one who is above him."""
"91","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""No one will enter Paradise because of his deeds."" They said: ""Not even you, O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him?"" He said: ""Not even I, unless Allah covers me with His mercy or His pardon encompasses me."""
"92","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah bin Yaman (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), a beggar stood up and began to ask (for help). The people remained silent. Then indeed, one man gave him something, so the people also gave him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever initiates a good way, and then it is adopted, for him is its reward and the reward of those who follow it, without their rewards being diminished in the least. And whoever establishes an evil way and it is adopted, upon him is its burden and the burden of those who follow him, without their burdens being diminished in the least."""
"93","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I do not recognize anything among you except that which I was familiar with during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), except your saying ‘La ilaha illallah’. We said: And not even the prayer, O Abu Hamzah!? He said: Indeed, you have performed the prayer (‘Asr) after the sun has set; was this the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? Then he said: Despite that, I have not seen any era better for the one who acts than your present time."
"94","It is narrated from Sayyidina Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the waiting period (‘iddah) of Sayyidah Zainab (bint Jahsh) (may Allah be pleased with her) was completed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Zaid (bin Harithah) (may Allah be pleased with him): “Go and give her my proposal of marriage.” He said: “I went and said: O Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her)! Rejoice, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has sent me, he is proposing marriage to you.” She said: “I will not do anything until I consult my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic.” She stood towards her mosque, and the Qur’an was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came, until he came to her without permission."
"95","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I and the Hour have been sent like these two."" And whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned the Hour, his cheeks would become red, his voice would become loud, and his anger would intensify, as if he were warning against an army: ""It may attack you in the morning, it may raid you in the evening."""
"96","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the 'Asr prayer during the day, then delivered a sermon to us until the sun set. He (peace and blessings be upon him) did not leave anything unmentioned that was to happen until the Day of Resurrection, except that he explained it to us. Whoever remembered it, remembered it, and whoever forgot it, forgot it. And when the sun was about to set, he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And the amount of your world that has passed and the amount that remains is like this day of yours: what has passed of it and what remains of it."""
"97","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that surely the Hour will definitely be established upon two men, while both of them will have their clothes in their hands."
"98","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How can I remain happy and at ease, while the one with the horn (trumpet) has certainly taken the horn in his mouth and is attentively listening, waiting for the command to blow, so he will blow it."" It seemed this was hard on the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so at that time he (peace and blessings be upon him) said to them: ""Say: 'Allah is sufficient for us and He is the best disposer of affairs, upon Allah alone we have placed our trust.'"""
"99","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked: ""What is the Sur?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""It is a horn in which it will be blown."""
"100","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will grasp the earth in His fist, then He will roll up the heavens in His right hand, then He will say: 'I am the King alone, where are the kings of the earth?'"""
"101","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: ﴿يَوْمَئِذٍ تُحَدِّثُ أَخْبَارَهَا﴾ (Az-Zalzalah: 4) “On that Day, it (the earth) will report its news.” He (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: “Do you know what its news are?” They said: Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) know best. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, its news are that it will testify about every servant, male and female, regarding what they did on its surface. It will say: On such and such day, he did such and such deed. So these are its news.”"
"102","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that regarding: ﴿يَوْمَ يَقُومُ النَّاسُ لِرَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ﴾ ""The Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds,"" (it means) until one of them will be submerged in his sweat up to half of his ears."
"103","It is like the previous hadith."
"104","It is narrated from the companion of the Messenger of Allah, Sayyiduna Miqdad (may Allah be pleased with him), that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""When the Day of Resurrection comes, the sun will be brought near to the servants, until it will be as close as one or two miles."" Salim (the narrator) said: I do not know which of the two miles is meant, whether it is the distance of the earth or the kohl stick with which kohl is applied to the eye. He (the Prophet) said: ""The sun will be melting them, and they will be in sweat according to their deeds. Among them will be one whom the sweat will seize up to his ankles, and among them will be one whom it will seize up to his knees, and among them will be one whom it will seize up to his waist, and among them will be one who will be bridled by it."" He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and he was pointing with his hand towards his mouth and saying: ""He will be bridled by it."""
"105","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting and the Qur'an will intercede for the servant. Fasting will say: My Lord! I kept him away from food and desires during the day, so accept my intercession for him. And the Qur'an will say: My Lord! I kept him away from sleep at night, so accept my intercession for him. Thus, both intercessions will be accepted."""
"106","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the people, the first judgment will be made concerning matters of blood (i.e., murder)."""
"107","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, a servant will be brought, as if he is a young goat, and he will be made to stand before Allah. Allah will say: I gave you, I bestowed upon you, and I showed you favor, so what did you do? He will say: O Lord! I gathered it, I increased it, and I left behind more than what I had (of wealth), so return me, I will bring all of it to You. Allah will say to him: Show Me what you sent ahead. He will say: I gathered it, I increased it, and I left behind more than what I had, so return me, I will bring all of it to You. Suddenly, that servant will not have sent ahead any good deed, so he will be driven towards the Fire."""
"108","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever is subjected to a detailed reckoning (questioning) will be destroyed."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Indeed, Allah the Exalted says: ﴿فَأَمَّا مَنْ أُوتِیَ کِتَابَهُ بِیَمِینِهِ فَسَوْفَ یُحَاسَبُ حِسَابًا یَسِیرًا﴾ (Al-Inshiqaq: 7,8) 'So as for he who is given his record in his right hand, soon he will be given an easy reckoning.'"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That will be only the presentation."""
"109","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, will select a man from my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection before all of creation. Ninety-nine registers will be opened before him, each register stretching as far as the eye can see. Then He will say to him: Do you deny anything from this? Did My recording angels wrong you? He will say: No, my Lord! Allah will say: Do you have any excuse or any good deed? The man will be overwhelmed with anxiety and say: No, my Lord! Allah will say: On the contrary, indeed you have one good deed with Us, and today you will not be wronged. Then a slip will be brought out for him, on which will be written: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and indeed Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger. Allah will say: Come to the scale. The man will say: O Lord! What is the worth of this slip compared to these registers? Allah will say: You will not be wronged. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then all the registers will be placed in one pan of the scale, and the registers will become light, and the slip will become heavy, for nothing can outweigh the name of Allah.”"
"110","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that meat was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and its foreleg was raised towards him, and he liked it. He (peace be upon him) tore from it with his teeth, then said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, I will be the leader of the people. Do you know how that will be? Allah will gather all the first and the last people in one plain. A caller will make them hear, the sight will encompass them, and the sun will come near. The people will reach such an extent of grief and distress that they will not be able to bear nor endure it. The people will say to one another: 'You must go to Adam (peace be upon him).' So they will come to Adam (peace be upon him) and say: 'You are the father of mankind, Allah created you with His own hand, and He breathed into you of His spirit, and He commanded the angels, so they prostrated to you. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in? Do you not see what has befallen us?' So Adam (peace be upon him) will say to them: 'Indeed, my Lord is so angry today as He has never been before, nor will He ever be so angry after this. And indeed, He forbade me from that tree, but I disobeyed Him. Woe to myself, woe to myself! Go to someone else, go to Nuh (Noah, peace be upon him).' Then they will come to Nuh (peace be upon him) and say: 'O Nuh! You are the first Messenger sent to the people of the earth, and Allah named you a grateful servant. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in? Do you not see what has befallen us?' He will say: 'Indeed, my Lord is so angry today as He has never been before, nor will He ever be so angry after this. And indeed, I had one supplication, and I used it against my people. Woe to myself, woe to myself! Go to someone else, go to Ibrahim (Abraham, peace be upon him).' They will come to Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and say: 'O Ibrahim! You are Allah's Prophet and His friend among the people of the earth. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in?' He will say to them: 'Indeed, my Lord is so angry today as He has never been before, nor will He ever be so angry after this. And indeed, I told three untrue statements.' Abu Hayyan (the narrator) mentioned them in the hadith. 'Woe to myself, woe to myself! Go to someone else, go to Musa (Moses, peace be upon him).' They will come to Musa (peace be upon him) and say: 'O Musa! You are Allah's Messenger. He preferred you over the people with His messages and His speech. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in?' He will say: 'Indeed, my Lord is so angry today as He has never been before, nor will He ever be so angry after this. And indeed, I killed a soul whom I was not commanded to kill. Woe to myself, woe to myself! Go to someone else, go to Isa (Jesus, peace be upon him).' They will come to Isa (peace be upon him) and say: 'O Isa! You are Allah's Messenger and His word which He cast to Maryam (Mary, peace be upon her), and a spirit from Him, and you spoke to the people in the cradle. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in?' Isa (peace be upon him) will say: 'Indeed, my Lord is so angry today as He has never been before, nor will He ever be so angry after this.' And he will not mention any sin. 'Woe to myself, woe to myself! Go to someone else, go to Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).' They will come to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and say: 'O Muhammad! You are the Messenger of Allah and the Seal of the Prophets. Allah has forgiven your past and future sins. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in?' I will go and come under the Throne, then I will fall in prostration to my Lord. Then Allah will open for me from His praise and beautiful words such as He has never opened for anyone before me. Then it will be said: 'O Muhammad! Raise your head, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted.' So I will raise my head and say: 'My Ummah, O my Lord, my Ummah, O my Lord, my Ummah, O my Lord!' Then it will be said to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): 'Admit from your Ummah through the rightmost gate of Paradise those who will have no reckoning, and they will share with the people in the other gates besides that.' Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'By Him in Whose hand is my soul! The distance between two panels of the gates of Paradise is like the distance between Makkah and Hajar, or between Makkah and Busra.'"""
"111","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned this hadith and said: “Isa (peace be upon him) will say: Shall I not direct you to the unlettered Prophet? So they will come to me, and Allah will permit me to stand, and my gathering will return with the purest fragrance that anyone has ever smelled, until I come to my Lord, and He will accept my intercession, and He will make light for me from the hair of my head to the nails of my feet. Then the disbelievers will say: Surely the believers have found someone to intercede for them, so who will intercede for us? They will say: None but Iblis, he is the one who led us astray. So they will come to him, and he will stand, and his gathering will return with the foulest stench that anyone has ever smelled, then he will lead them into Hell and at that time he will say: ‘And when the matter (of Paradise or Hell) has been decided, Satan will say: Indeed, Allah promised you the promise of truth, and I promised you but I betrayed you.’”"
"112","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr and Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I will be the first to be granted permission to prostrate on the Day of Resurrection, and I will be the first to be granted permission to raise my head. I will look ahead and recognize my Ummah among the nations, and I will look to my right and recognize my Ummah among the nations, and I will look to my left and recognize my Ummah among the nations, and I will look behind me and recognize my Ummah among the nations.” A man asked, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! How will you recognize your Ummah among the nations, from Nuh (peace be upon him) up to your own Ummah?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: “Their faces, hands, and feet will be radiant due to the marks of ablution; no one else among the nations will have this, and I will recognize them. Indeed, their books of deeds will be given to them in their right hands, and I will recognize them by their foreheads due to the marks of prostration on their faces, and I will recognize them by the light that will be running before them and on their right side.”"
"113","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""On the Day of Resurrection, my Ummah will come like the night or like a flood that sweeps people away all at once. Then the angels will say: Surely, those who came with Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) are more than those who came with the rest of the communities."""
"114","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, for every prophet there is a supplication which is accepted, and surely he has already supplicated with it, and indeed I have kept my supplication hidden for the intercession of my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection."""
"115","Buhz bin Hakeem narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""Indeed, you will complete seventy nations on the Day of Resurrection; you will be the best among them and the most honorable in the sight of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"116","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “We are the last to come, but the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, and that is because the People of the Book were given this (Friday) before us, and we were given it after them. So this is their day about which they differed, so Allah guided us to it, and thus they follow us in this regard. The next day for the Jews is (Saturday), and for the Christians the day after that (Sunday).”"
"117","Sayyiduna Abu Barzah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that indeed he heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: “Indeed, among my Ummah are some who will venerate the Fire, until they become one of its pillars, and indeed among my Ummah are also those who will intercede for more people than (the tribes of) Rabi’ah and Mudar.”"
"118","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “A group from my Ummah, whose (number) will be seventy thousand, will enter Paradise; their faces will be shining like the light of the moon on the fourteenth night.” Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that Ukasha bin Mihsan (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up, lifted the striped cloak that was over him, and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Pray to Allah that He includes me among them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O Allah! Include him among them.” Then a man from the Ansar stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Pray for me that Allah includes me among them. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Ukasha (may Allah be pleased with him) has preceded you in this matter.”"
"119","Sayyiduna Fadala bin Ubaid and Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the Day of Resurrection comes and Allah has finished judging the creation, two men will remain. They will be ordered to be taken towards the Fire, so one of them will turn and look back. The Compeller (Allah) will say: 'Return him,' so he will be returned, and it will be said to him: 'Why did you look back?' He will say: 'I was hoping that He would admit me to Paradise.'"" He said: ""He will be ordered to be taken towards Paradise."" He said: ""He will say: 'Indeed, my Lord has given me (so much) that if I were to feed all the people of Paradise, it would not decrease what I have (to feed) in the least.'"" Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned this, happiness could be seen on his face."
"120","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, among those who were admitted into the Fire, the cries and wails of two men became very intense. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: Take these two out. When both were taken out, it was said to them: For what reason did your cries and wails become so intense? Both said: We did this so that You may have mercy on us. He said: My mercy for you is that both of you go and throw yourselves into the Fire at the place where you were. Both will go; one of them will throw himself into the Fire, and Allah will make it coolness and safety for him, and the other will stand and will not throw himself in. The Lord will ask him: What prevented you from throwing yourself in, just as your companion did? He will say: O Lord! I hoped that after You took me out, You would not return me to it again. The Lord will say to him: For you is your hope. So both of them will enter Paradise by His mercy.”"
"121","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (Sa'd bin Malik bin Sinan) رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""Indeed, Allah the Exalted will say to the people of Paradise: O people of Paradise! They will say: O our Lord! We are present again and again. He will say: Are you pleased? They will say: What is there that we should not be pleased, and surely You have given us that which You have not given to anyone among Your creation. He will say: I will give you something even better than that. They will say: O Lord! What could be better than this? He will say: I make My pleasure lawful for you, so I will never be displeased with you after this."""
"122","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first group to enter Paradise will have faces like the moon on the night it is full. They will neither spit in it, nor blow their noses, nor relieve themselves. Their vessels will be of gold and their combs will be of gold and silver, and their incense burners will be of aloes-wood. Their sweat will be musk, and each of them will have two wives, the marrow of whose shins will be visible from behind the flesh due to their beauty. There will be no differences among them, nor mutual hatred; their hearts will be as one heart, and they will glorify Allah morning and evening."""
"123","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We are the last to come, but on the Day of Resurrection we will be the foremost. The first group of my Ummah to enter Paradise will be seventy thousand, who will have no reckoning. Each of them will have a face like the full moon of the fourteenth night. Then those who follow them will be like the brightest star in the sky. After that, there will be several ranks."""
"124","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that: “Indeed, if even a (blessing) of Paradise less than the size of a small fingernail were to be revealed, then everything in the surroundings of the heavens and the earth would become adorned and beautified. And if indeed any one man from among the people of Paradise were to look out and his bracelets became visible, then surely their light would outshine the light of the sun, just as the sun extinguishes the light of the stars.”"
"125","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, the people of Paradise will see each other in ranks of superiority from their lofty chambers, just as you see the eastern or western star that is about to set or rise on the horizon."" They said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Will those only be the Prophets?"" He replied, ""Why not! By Him in Whose hand is my soul! And there will also be those who believed in Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) and affirmed the Messengers."""
"126","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The lowest among the people of Paradise will be the one who will have eighty servants and seventy-two wives. For him, a tent of pearls, emeralds, and rubies will be set up, as large as the distance between Jabiyah and Sana‘a.”"
"127","With this same chain (this hadith is also narrated that) the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever among the people of Paradise dies, whether young or old, will be returned to the age of thirty years in Paradise; they will never be older than that. And the people of Hell will also be of the same age."""
"128","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He will see his own face in the cheek of her (the houri) more clear than in a mirror, and indeed, the lowest pearl that will be upon her will surely illuminate what is between the east and the west, and in reality, there will be seventy garments upon her, his gaze will pass through them, until he will see the marrow of her shin from behind."""
"129","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Indeed, in Paradise there is a great tree such that a rider could travel in its shade for seventy—or he said, one hundred—years, and it is the tree of eternity."""
"130","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he reports from the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has said: I have prepared for My righteous servants that which no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has never even occurred to the heart of any human."""
"131","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the people of Paradise will proceed towards Paradise and the people of the Fire towards the Fire, death will be brought and placed between Paradise and the Fire, then it will be slaughtered. Then a caller will announce: O people of Paradise! (now) there is no death, O people of the Fire! (now) there is no death. So the people of Paradise will increase in their happiness towards their joy, and the people of the Fire will increase in their sorrow towards their grief."""
"132","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I (the narrator) think that he narrated it as marfu‘: ""Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in the form of a speckled ram, and it will be made to stand between Paradise and the Fire. It will be said: O people of Paradise! This is death. O people of the Fire! This is death. Then it will be slaughtered while they are looking on."" If anyone were to die of joy, the people of Paradise would surely die, and if anyone were to die of grief, the people of the Fire would surely die."
"133","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If indeed a stone like this""—and he (peace be upon him) pointed towards his skull—""is thrown from the sky towards the earth, and that is a distance of five hundred years, then surely it would reach before nightfall. And if indeed it is let go from the end of that chain, then surely it would keep falling for forty years, day and night, before reaching (the bottom of Hell)."""
"134","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""O people! Weep, and if you do not weep, then make a weeping face. Surely, the people of the Fire will weep in the Fire until their tears flow down their faces like small streams of irrigation, until their tears run out, then blood will flow. Their eyes will be wounded, and if indeed boats are sailed in them, they will certainly sail."""
"135","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “ ﴿وَهُمْ فِيهَا كَالِحُونَ﴾ (Al-Mu’minun: 104) ‘And they will be grimacing therein.’ He said: The fire will burn him, so his upper lip will shrink until it reaches the middle of his head, and his lower lip will hang down until it reaches his navel.”"
"136","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This fire of yours, which the son of Adam kindles, is one part out of seventy parts of the (fire of) Hell."" They (the Companions, may Allah be pleased with them) said: By Allah! If it were (just) this (worldly fire), it would certainly be sufficient. O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! He said: ""Indeed, it has been increased by sixty-nine parts besides this, all of them like its heat."""
"137","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who reports from the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Indeed, hot water will certainly be poured over their heads, it will penetrate through the skull until it reaches the belly, and whatever is in the belly will be brought out, until it comes out from his feet, and this is what melting means. Then he will be returned to the way he was."""
"138","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding the statement of Allah, the Exalted: “ ﴿وَيُسْقَى مِنْ مَاءٍ صَدِيدٍ يَتَجَرَّعُهُ﴾ (Ibrahim: 17) ‘And he will be given to drink of pus, which he will sip with difficulty.’” He (the Prophet) said: When it is brought near to him, it will be extremely unpleasant to him, and when it is brought close to him, it will scorch his face and the skin of his head will fall off. When he drinks it, it will cut his intestines until it comes out from his back. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was saying: “ ﴿وَسُقُوا مَاءً حَمِيمًا فَقَطَّعَ أَمْعَاءَهُمْ﴾ (Muhammad: 15) ‘And they will be given boiling water to drink, so it will cut up their intestines.’” And Allah, the Exalted, said: “ ﴿وَإِنْ يَسْتَغِيثُوا يُغَاثُوا بِمَاءٍ كَالْمُهْلِ يَشْوِي الْوُجُوهَ بِئْسَ الشَّرَابُ وَسَاءَتْ مُرْتَفَقًا﴾ (Al-Kahf: 29) ‘And if they call for relief, they will be relieved with water like molten brass, which will scald their faces. What a terrible drink and what an evil resting place!’”"
"139","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That water will be like molten copper, like the dregs of oil; when it is brought near, the skin of the face will fall off."""
"140","And with this chain of narration, it is reported that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the enclosures of the Fire are four thick walls, each wall is a distance of forty years."""
"141","And it is narrated with the same chain that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""If indeed a bucket of pus were poured out in the world, it would surely make the people of the world foul-smelling."""
"142","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I saw some people whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I asked, 'O Jibreel (peace be upon him)! Who are these?' He replied: 'They are the preachers of your ummah who used to enjoin righteousness upon the people but forgot their own selves, and they used to recite the Book (as well). Do they not then understand?'"""
"143","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in Hell there is certainly a valley which is called 'Lamlum.' Indeed, the valleys of Hell seek refuge from its heat."""
"144","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that ""'Wail' is a valley in Hell; a disbeliever will keep falling in it for forty years before reaching its depth, and 'Sa'ud' is a mountain of fire; he will keep climbing it for seventy years, then will fall into the fire."""
"145","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that indeed a Jew crushed the head of a girl between two stones. She was asked, ""Who did this to you?"" It was said, ""Was it so-and-so or so-and-so?"" until the name of that Jew was mentioned, and she indicated with her head, meaning yes. So that Jew was called, and he confessed (to the crime). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered regarding him, so his head was also crushed between two stones, or he said, with a stone."
"146","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For the fingers, (the blood money is) ten (camels) each, and for the wound that exposes the bone, (the blood money is) five (camels)."""
"147","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who reports from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""This and this are equal,"" and Shu’bah (the narrator) pointed towards the little finger and the thumb."
"148","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The fingers are equal."" I said to Ghalib Tammar, ""Is it ten camels in compensation for each finger?"" He said: ""Yes."""
"149","Haram bin Sa’d bin Muheysah and Sa’eed bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on them) narrate that indeed the she-camel of Bara’ bin ‘Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) entered the garden of a people and caused damage. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ruled that “Indeed, the protection of wealth during the day is upon its owners, and surely, upon the owners of livestock is (the compensation for) what their animals cause at night.”"
"150","Sayyiduna Mughira bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that indeed two women who were under one man from Banu Huzail (as wives), one of them struck the other with a tent pole, causing her pregnancy to miscarry. They brought the dispute to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and said: How can we pay blood money for one who neither cried nor screamed, neither drank nor ate? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Is this rhymed speech like the rhymed speech of the Bedouins?” Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) ruled for the freeing of a slave, and made it incumbent upon the woman’s ‘asaba (male relatives)."
"151","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that Ya'la bin Munabbih mentioned about the person who bites and his tooth breaks, there is no compensation (diyah) for him. He mentioned this matter before the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no compensation for you."""
"152","This same hadith has been narrated through another chain, in which Ibn Ya'la narrates from his father."
"153","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that indeed a man was brought to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) who had drunk wine. The Prophet (peace be upon him) struck him with two sticks, about forty times. He said, and this is what Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) did. Then when Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was (the caliph), he consulted the people. Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the lightest prescribed punishment among the hudud is eighty lashes, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the order regarding this."
"154","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that a drunkard was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He said, ""I did not drink wine; I only drank (a beverage made from) raisins and dates in a gourd vessel."" So he was reprimanded with hands and shoes, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade (the use of) gourd vessels and mixing raisins and dates (for drinking)."
"155","Sayyiduna Abu Umayyah Makhzumi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that indeed a thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), who confessed (to the crime) and no goods were found with him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: ""I do not think that you have committed theft."" He said: Why not. He (the Prophet) again said: ""I do not think that you have committed theft."" He said: Why not. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take him away and cut off his hand, then bring him back to me."" So they cut off his hand and then brought him back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say: I seek forgiveness from Allah and turn to Him in repentance."" He said: I seek forgiveness from Allah and turn to Him in repentance. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Accept his repentance."""
"156","Abdullah bin Muhairiz said that I asked Fadala bin Ubaid (may Allah be pleased with him) about hanging the thief's hand around his neck, so he said that this is the Sunnah. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) cut off the hand of a thief and hung his hand around his neck."
"157","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that it was said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What is your opinion about the enclosures of goats in the field? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For them, there is compensation like them, and there are lashes as punishment, and the hand is not cut off for anything among the animals except for that which the enclosure provides space for, and it reaches the value of a shield, then the hand is cut off for it. And for anything among the fruits, (the hand is not cut off) except for that which the threshing floor (the place where fruits are gathered) provides space for. Whoever takes from the threshing floor and it reaches the value of a shield, then the hand is to be cut off for it."""
"158","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has exempted the hand-cutting punishment from the highway robber, the snatcher, and the betrayer."
"159","The noble wife of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), narrates that indeed a man from a place called Kada’, who was accused of theft by the people of Makkah, came to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) during his caliphate. He showed kindness to him, to the extent that Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) sent a zakat collector from among the Ansar and sent him along with that man, and continued to show him compassion for nearly two months. Then he came back, and his camel was being made to sit down. The zakat collector had already cut off his hand. (Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said:) When Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) saw him, his eyes overflowed with tears and he said, “Woe to you, what happened to you?” He replied, “O Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with you)! He found me near the obligatory (zakat) and in that he cut off my hand.” Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “May Allah destroy the one who cut off your hand in this obligation which he kept at his side. By Allah! Indeed, I see him betraying in more than thirty obligations. By the One in Whose hand is my soul! If you are truly truthful, I will surely take retribution for you from him.” Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I was in the same house where I was before his hand was cut off in the house of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). That (thief) would stand and pray at night, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) would toss and turn restlessly on his bed, and when he heard his recitation, his eyes would overflow with tears and he would say, “May Allah cut off the hand of the one who cut off his hand.” While we were in this state, Asma bint Umais (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), came at night; theft had occurred in her house. When Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) led the morning prayer, he stood among the people and said, “Indeed, the people of the tribe came at night, and they have been robbed. So go out and search for their belongings.” She said: That handless man sought permission to enter upon us, so Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) granted him permission, and I was sitting behind a veil. He said, “O Abu Bakr! Was there no one keeping watch at night?” Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, “Yes.” So he raised his sound hand and his severed hand and said, “O Allah! Disgrace the thief of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him).” She said: By Allah! The day had not yet fully dawned when the theft was discovered from that very house. He was brought to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said, “Woe to you! By Allah! You know nothing about Allah. Take him away and cut off his foot.”"
"160","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she reports from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that indeed he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The thief's hand is to be cut off for a quarter of a dinar."""
"161","This hadith has been narrated with another chain of transmission."
"162","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who reports from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that indeed he (peace be upon him) said: ""A hand was cut off for a shield, the price of which was three dirhams."""
"163","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed a man from the (tribe of) Aslam came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he informed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he had committed adultery, and he testified against himself four times. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave the order regarding him, and he was stoned to death, and he was married."
"164","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that indeed Ma'iz bin Malik came to a man who was called Hiraak and said: O Hiraak! Indeed, another has certainly committed adultery, what is your opinion? He said: Go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Before the Qur'an is revealed about you, he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him that indeed he had committed adultery. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him. He informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) again, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him. This happened four times (he turned his face away). When it was the fourth time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to be stoned. When he was stoned, he took refuge by a tree, so he was killed. A man said to his companion: He was killed just as a dog is killed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a (swollen due to death) donkey and said to both of them: ""Tear off the flesh of this donkey."" Both of them said: O Messenger of Allah! This is a foul-smelling carcass, can its flesh be torn off? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What you have reached about your brother is more foul-smelling. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he is indeed diving in the rivers of Paradise."" It is said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hiraas: ""O Hiraas! Why did you not have mercy on him?"""
"165","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Jews brought two Jews (a man and a woman) to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: “Will you establish the prescribed punishment on both of them?” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Why did you not establish the prescribed punishment on both of them?” They said: “If we have control, we do it, and if it is lost, we do not.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Bring me your two greatest scholars,” so they brought the two sons of Surya. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to both of them: “Do you have more knowledge than those who come after you?” They said: “These (Jews) think so.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I adjure you by Allah who revealed the Torah to Musa (peace be upon him), do you not find this prescribed punishment in the Torah?” Both of them said: “We find in the Torah that indeed, when a man is in seclusion with a woman in a house and both are caught, then both are let go and there is punishment in it, and if it is found that he is lying with her, then he is let go and there is punishment in it, and if he fully penetrates her as the kohl stick enters the kohl container, then there is stoning in it.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave the order regarding both of them and they were stoned. It is said that before this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had stoned Ma'iz bin Malik Al-Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him), who had testified against himself four times, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave the order regarding him and he was stoned. Shu’bi (may Allah have mercy on him) said that Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) showed me the place where he was stoned."
"166","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, stoned Ma'iz and did not mention lashes."
"167","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Aslami came to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and confessed to adultery. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perhaps you kissed, or touched with your hand, or looked."""
"168","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One prescribed punishment that is carried out on earth is better for the people of the earth than thirty mornings (days) of rain."""
"169","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a disabled person was brought to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was near the threshing floors (places where fruits are gathered) of Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him). He confessed (to adultery), so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Beat him with a bunch of date-palm branches.” That is, with twigs that have date-palm branches."
"170","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""When the slave-girl of any one of you commits adultery, he should flog her and not set her free. If she commits adultery, he should flog her; if she commits adultery, he should flog her; if she commits adultery, then he should sell her, even if it is in exchange for a rope of hair or a braid of hair."""
"171","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Khalid al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) both narrate that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about a slave-girl: if she commits adultery and is not married, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If she commits adultery, then flog her; then if she commits adultery, then flog her; then if she commits adultery, then flog her; then sell her, even if it is in exchange for a rope of hair."" After the third or fourth time. And ""dhafeer"" refers to a rope."
"172","Ash'ath bin Qais said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) among some people of Kindah, and they considered me to be their most virtuous man. I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Indeed, we think that you (peace be upon him) are from among us? He (peace be upon him) said: ""We are Banu Nadir bin Kinana; we neither slander our mother with a false accusation nor do we deny our father."" Ash'ath said: By Allah! Whenever I heard of any man who denied the lineage of any man of Quraysh from Nadr bin Kinana, I would certainly administer the legal punishment of lashes to him."
"173","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim cannot be the heir of a disbeliever, nor can a disbeliever be the heir of a Muslim."""
"174","Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim cannot be the heir of a disbeliever."""
"175","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Followers of two (different) religions cannot inherit from each other."""
"176","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) paid off the debt before the bequest, although you recite, ﴿مِنْ بَعْدِ وَصِيَّةٍ يُوصَى بِهَا أَوْ دَيْنٍ﴾ (An-Nisa: 12) ""After any bequest he may have made or debt (has been paid)."" And indeed, full brothers inherit from one another, not half-brothers. That is, brothers from both the father and mother, not just from the father."
"177","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that indeed the freed slave of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was cutting date palm branches when he fell and died, and he left behind some inheritance. This was reported to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: “Does he have any children or friends?” They said: No. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Look for someone from the people of the town and entrust this (wealth) to him.”"
"178","Khalid bin Abi Hayan said that there was a woman from Banu Dinar who had set me free, then she married among Banu Salamah and had children from them, then she (the one who set me free) passed away. I entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them), so some people said, ""O Abu Abdullah! This is the one who is going to ask you about your 'wala'."" I said, ""I seek refuge with Allah! I am the freed slave of such-and-such Dinariyah woman."" So Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Yes, O son of my sister! Indeed, I bear witness that I certainly heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Whoever makes anyone other than his masters his master, he has removed the noose of faith from his neck,' and he was gesturing with his hand like this three times."""
"179","Saeed bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that indeed a woman came to Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), demanding her inheritance from her husband’s (blood money), so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “Blood money is only for the ‘Asabah (male agnates), and I do not know of anything for you.” And Mu’ammar said that he understood that blood money is only for the ‘Asabah, because they are the ones who pay it. Then he consulted the people and said: “Does anyone have any knowledge about this?” So Dahhak bin Sufyan al-Kilabi (may Allah be pleased with him) said that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wrote to me that I should make the wife of Ashyam Dhibabi an heir from her husband’s blood money, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) made her an heir."
"180","Al-Zuhri, may Allah have mercy on him, narrates that indeed the killing of Ashim was accidental killing."
"181","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) found Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was swearing by his father. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah forbids you from swearing by your forefathers. So whoever wants to swear an oath, let him swear by Allah or remain silent."""
"182","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears by other than Allah..."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) spoke very harshly about this."
"183","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would often swear by this oath: He (peace be upon him) would say, ""No, by the One Who turns the hearts."""
"184","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that indeed the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) heard Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: ""By your father!"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah forbids you from swearing by your fathers."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""By Allah! After that, I never swore by them, neither intentionally nor quoting someone."""
"185","Umar bin Abdur Rahman bin Awf narrates from an Ansari man among the companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) that indeed, on the day of the conquest of Makkah, a man from the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Indeed, I have made a vow that if Allah grants victory of Makkah to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and the believers, then I will surely lead prayer in Bayt al-Maqdis, and indeed I have found a man from the people of Sham here among the Quraysh, going and returning with me, to be insignificant."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Pray here."" That man repeated his statement three times, and each time the Prophet (peace be upon him) told him: ""Pray here."" Then, when he repeated his statement a fourth time, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Then go and pray there. By the One Who sent Muhammad (peace be upon him) with the truth, if you pray here, it will certainly be as if you have performed your prayer in Bayt al-Maqdis."" Ibn Jurayj (may Allah have mercy on him) said that the man was Shuraid bin Suwayd bin Sadaf from the tribe of Banu Thaqif."
"186","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade making vows and said, ""Indeed, it does not avert anything, and through it only something is taken out from a miserly person."""
"187","The same hadith has been narrated through another chain."
"188","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no vow in disobedience (to Allah), and its expiation is the expiation for an oath."""
"189","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Indeed, I had made a vow in the days of ignorance that I would observe i'tikaf for one night in Masjid al-Haram. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fulfill your vow."""
"190","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that when we returned from Hunayn, Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about the vow he had made in the days of ignorance, that is, the vow of i'tikaf (seclusion in the mosque) for one day. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed him to fulfill it."
"191","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that indeed Sa’d bin Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) sought a verdict from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding a vow that was upon his mother, and she passed away before fulfilling it, so the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed him to fulfill it."
"192","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not say (in this manner): 'What Allah willed and so-and-so willed,' rather you should say: 'What Allah willed, then so-and-so willed.'"""
"193","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that a man came to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and spoke to him with some words and said: ""Whatever Allah wills and you will."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have you made me equal to Allah? Say: Whatever Allah alone wills."""
"194","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), we used to eat the meat of horses."
"195","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade us from (eating) the meat of donkeys and commanded us regarding the meat of horses."
"196","Sayyida Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that we slaughtered a horse during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and ate its meat."
"197","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the meat of domestic donkeys on the day of Khaybar."
"198","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the day of Khaybar, we reached the slave women, and we used to practice 'azl (withdrawal) with them, and we were searching to see if any of their families would pay their ransom. So some of us said to others, ""You are doing this while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) is among you?"" So we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned this before him. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Not every drop of water (semen) produces a child. When Allah decides a matter, it happens."" He said that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by some pots that were boiling, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: ""What meat is this?"" We said: ""Donkey meat."" He asked: ""Domestic or wild?"" We said: ""No, rather domestic."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said to us: ""Pour it out."" So we poured it out, and indeed we were hungry and desired it. He said: ""And we were commanded to tie the mouths of the water skins with a rope."""
"199","Sayyiduna Abu Tha’labah al-Khushani (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the meat of donkeys and every predatory animal with fangs."
"200","Sayyiduna Abu Tha’labah al-Khushani, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade every beast of prey with fangs among the predatory animals."
"201","The same hadith has been narrated through another chain."
"202","Yazid bin Abdullah Sa'di (may Allah have mercy on him) says that I asked Sa'id bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) about the badger, so he said: ""Indeed, its consumption is not permissible, and does anyone eat it?"" I said: ""Indeed, some people of my tribe pick it up and eat it."" He said: ""Surely, its consumption is not permissible."" A sheikh who was with him said: ""If you wish, I will narrate to you what I heard Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) say."" He said: ""I heard him say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade every act of highway robbery, every act of snatching, every animal killed as a target, and every beast of prey with fangs."" Sa'id bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ""You have spoken the truth."""
"203","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that he saw a rabbit and went out in search of it and became tired. Then I caught it and brought it to Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him). He slaughtered it and sent me with its thigh to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) accepted it."
"204","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The snake is a transgressor, and the badger is a transgressor, and the mouse is a transgressor, and the crow is a transgressor."" It is said that a man asked Qasim bin Muhammad, ""Can the crow be eaten?"" He replied, ""After the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), it is a transgressor. Who would eat it?"""
"205","Sayyiduna Khalid bin Walid, the Sword of Allah (may Allah be pleased with him), narrates that he went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to the house of Sayyidah Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her). She was the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and the maternal aunt of Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). He found roasted lizard there, which her sister Hafidah bint Harith had brought from Najd. She presented that lizard to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he (peace and blessings be upon him) would rarely extend his hand towards food until he was informed about it and its name was mentioned for him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) extended his hand towards the lizard, but one of the women present said, ""Inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about what you have presented to him."" They said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! This is lizard."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) withdrew his hand from the lizard. Khalid bin Walid (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Is lizard forbidden, O Messenger of Allah?"" He replied, ""No, but it is not found in the land of my people, and my nature dislikes it."" Khalid (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""So I pulled it towards me and ate it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was looking at me and did not forbid me."""
"206","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) found that a young goat which was with them was missing, so she informed him that indeed it had died. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why did you not take its skin and benefit from it?"""
"207","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Benefit from the skins of dead animals when they are tanned."""
"208","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the year of conquest, and he was in Makkah, saying: ""Indeed, Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) have forbidden the trade of intoxicants, carrion, and the flesh of swine."" It was asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What is your opinion about the fat of carrion? For indeed, it is used to oil water skins, it is used to oil leather, and people use it to light lamps."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No, it is forbidden."" May Allah destroy the Jews, for when Allah made fat forbidden for them, they melted it, then sold it and consumed its price."""
"209","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade branding on the face and hitting on the face."
"210","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade killing the ant, the honeybee, the hoopoe, and the shrike."
"211","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""In the colony of ants, an ant bit a prophet, so he burned that colony. Allah revealed to him: 'One ant bit you, and you destroyed a whole community among the communities that used to glorify (Me).'"""
"212","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that my mother asked my father for a gift for me from his wealth. He delayed it for a year, then it appeared to him to give me the gift, and indeed she (my mother) said, “I will not be pleased until you make the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) a witness to the gift you give my son.” So he took my hand, and I was a child in those days, and brought me to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Indeed, his mother, the daughter of Rawaha, has been insisting for a year that I give this son of mine a gift, and now it has appeared to me to give him the gift. O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! She feels that you should be made a witness.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O Bashir! Do you have any children other than him?” He said: Yes. I think the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do not make me a witness to this.”"
"213","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrated, and he was delivering a sermon: My father took me to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) so that he could make him a witness to the gift he had given me. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do you have any other sons besides him?” He replied: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Treat them equally.”"
"214","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no bad example for us. The one who takes back his gift is like a dog that returns to its vomit."""
"215","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that indeed a man gave a gift, then took it back, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is like the example of a dog, which eats until when it is full, it vomits what is in its belly, then turns towards it and eats it."" And Amr bin Shu'aib (may Allah have mercy on him) said that I was present with Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him), and he narrated this hadith for a man during his caliphate."
"216","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrated it as marfu‘ to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “It is not lawful for a man to give a gift and then take it back, except for a father regarding what he gives to his son. And the example of one who gives a gift and then takes it back is like a dog that eats, and when it is full, it vomits, then returns to its vomit.”"
"217","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both), who reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Do not make anything as Raqba; whoever makes something as Raqba, it belongs to him. And do not make anything as Umra; whoever makes something as Umra, it belongs to him."""
"218","Muhammad bin Ali said that Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me: ""What do you say about 'Umra (a type of gift)?"" I said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) accepted it."" Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""I bear witness that indeed I heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"219","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Umra is for the heir."""
"220","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Umra is permissible."""
"221","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Umra is permissible for his heirs, or it is the inheritance of his heirs."""
"222","Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates a similar hadith from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"223","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates a similar hadith from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"224","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: ""It is not permissible for any woman to give a gift except with the permission of her husband."""
"225","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of the person who takes back his charity is like the example of a dog who returns to its vomit and eats it."""
"226","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that indeed Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) acquired land in Khaybar, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Indeed, I have acquired land in Khaybar. By Allah! I have never acquired any wealth that is more precious to me than this. What do you advise me? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you wish, give it as charity and keep its original (property) withheld."" So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave it as charity (in such a way that) its original could neither be sold, nor gifted, nor inherited. He gave it as charity for the poor, relatives, in the way of Allah, for freeing slaves, for travelers and guests. There is no sin upon the one who manages it, to eat from it in a good manner and to feed a friend, but he should not make it his own wealth. I mentioned this hadith to Muhammad, and when I reached here, ""he should not make it his own wealth,"" he said that there should be no one asking for wealth in it. So a man informed me that indeed he had read that note, in which it was written that there should be no one asking for wealth in it."
"227","Ubaid bin Abi Al-Ja’d, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated: Shurahbil bin Simt called Marrah bin Ka’b or Ka’b bin Marrah and said: Narrate to me a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and fear (Allah). So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: “Whoever frees a Muslim (male) slave, Allah will free each of his limbs from the Fire in exchange for each limb of that (slave), and whoever frees a Muslim woman (slave-girl), Allah will free each of his limbs from the Fire in exchange for each limb of hers.”"
"228","Ghuraif bin Iyash bin Farqad Dailami said that I came to Wasila bin Asqa’ (may Allah be pleased with him), so (Kilaab) said to him, “Narrate to us a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).” He said, “Yes, we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for the expedition of Tabuk. A group from Banu Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so one of our companions said to him, ‘Indeed, he has made it obligatory.’ So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘He should free a neck like it in this. For every limb of his, Allah will free a (corresponding) limb of his from the Fire.’”"
"229","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say regarding a male or female slave who is jointly owned by several partners, and one of them frees his share, that it becomes obligatory to free the entire slave, if the person who freed his share possesses enough wealth to cover the value (of the remaining shares). The fair value will be assessed from his wealth, he will return the shares to the other partners, and the one who is freed will have his way made completely free. Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated this from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"230","Sulaiman bin Yasar narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If a man and another person share ownership of a slave, and one of them frees his share, then it is obligatory upon the one who freed (his share), if he has wealth, that the remaining value of the slave be paid."""
"231","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated a similar hadith from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). Takhrij: Sahih Bukhari, Al-Shirkah: 14, Chapter: Partnership in Slaves: 5/103."
"232","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he reports from the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: ""Whoever frees a share of his slave, it is obligatory upon him to free him completely from his own wealth. But if he does not have wealth, then the slave's price will be determined justly, then he will be required to strive (to pay it off), and no hardship will be imposed upon him."""
"233","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Utbah bin Abi Waqqas said to his brother Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him)—and Utbah was a disbeliever and Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) was a Muslim—“Indeed, I urge you that the son of Zam’ah’s slave woman is my son, and Zam’ah was an individual from Banu Amir bin Lu’ayy. When you meet the son of Zam’ah’s slave woman, take him.” Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the day of the conquest (of Makkah) came, Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) met the son of Zam’ah’s slave woman and said, “My nephew,” and embraced him. Abd bin Zam’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Rather, he is my brother; he was born on my father’s bed, from his slave woman.” So both of them took the dispute to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and Abd bin Zam’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Rather, he is your brother; he was born on my father’s bed, from his slave woman.” Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) looked and saw a resemblance to Utbah, which people had not clearly noticed before. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “He is for you, O Abd bin Zam’ah! The child is for the (owner of the) bed, and O Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her)! Observe veil from him.” So she did not see him until she passed away."
"234","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates that indeed a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""Indeed, I have a slave woman and I intend to go to her and prevent her (from becoming pregnant)."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! Indeed, that which Allah wills, this thing will certainly not prevent it,"" or he said: ""That which Allah wills, nothing can prevent it."" Then that man came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Indeed, my slave woman has given birth to a child."""
"235","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), a Bedouin from Banu Fazarah came and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Indeed, my wife has given birth to a black child, and at that time he was denying it, he only said this to disassociate himself from the (child). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do you have camels?” He said: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “What is their color?” He said: Red. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: “Are there any among them that are brownish?” He said: Yes, there are ash-colored camels among them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: “Where did these come from?” He said: I do not know, except that some lineage must have drawn them out. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “And perhaps some lineage has drawn out this (child) as well.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) refused to grant him permission to disassociate himself from the child."
"236","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that indeed a man freed his slave despite being in debt, so he became needy. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) seized him and said: ""Who will buy him from me?"" So Naeem bin Abdullah bought him for such and such amount, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) handed him over to him."
"237","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling “wala” and gifting it, but indeed Ubaidullah forgot to mention gifting or did not mention it."
"238","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Barirah came and said: Indeed, my masters have written a contract of emancipation with me for seven uqiyahs, one uqiyah (forty dirhams) to be paid each year, so please help me. She (Aisha) said: If your masters are pleased that I pay them the entire amount at once, I will do so, but your ""wala"" (right of allegiance) will be mine. She went to her masters, but they refused this, so she came back to Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was with her, and said: Indeed, I offered it to them, but they refused, except that the ""wala"" would be theirs. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) heard this, he asked Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), and she informed him of the whole matter. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then buy her and set her free, and stipulate the condition of 'wala' for them, for indeed 'wala' is for the one who sets free."" So Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) did so. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among the people in the latter part of the day, praised and glorified Allah, and then said: ""Amma ba'd! What is the matter with some men among you who impose conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Any condition that is not in the Book of Allah is invalid, even if there are a hundred such conditions. The decision of Allah is more rightful and the condition of Allah is stronger. So what is the matter with one of you who says he has set someone free but the 'wala' is his? 'Wala' is only for the one who sets free."""
"239","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever becomes the owner of a relative, then he is free."""
"240","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""There are three people: it is a right upon Allah to help all of them: the one who strives in the path of Allah, the one who marries seeking chastity, and the slave who has made a contract for his freedom and intends to fulfill it."""
"241","Sha'bi (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Qarza intended to go to Iraq with some people from Banu Abd al-Ashhal. Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) also set out with them, requested water, performed ablution, and said: ""Do you know why I have come out with you?"" They said: ""Because of your love for us and our right."" He said: ""Indeed, you have a right, but I have come to say one thing: narrate few ahadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and I am your partner in this (adherence)."" (Sha'bi) said: ""After this statement of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), I would not narrate hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."""
"242","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: (Sha'bi said) Then he (Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him) began to tremble with anxiety, or he said that he started to shake, and said: either above this or less than this, and like this."
"243","Amr bin Maymoon (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that I used to come and go to Abdullah bin Masood (may Allah be pleased with him) for a year. I did not hear him say during that time that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: except for one hadith which he certainly narrated, and when he began to say, ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said,"" he was overtaken by great anxiety, to the extent that I saw drops of sweat dripping from his forehead. Then he said: If Allah wills, or above this, or like this, or something close to it. (The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said)."
"244","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: We used to memorize hadith, and the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to be remembered, until they (the Companions, may Allah be pleased with them) faced every hardship for its sake and overcame it."
"245","Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah have mercy on him) says that I set out from Madinah to Makkah with Sa’d bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), and I did not hear him narrate even a single hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), until we returned. Hammad said that (he did so) out of reverence and the gravity of narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and our condition is such that we narrate such and such (hadiths) between ourselves and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and we waste them."
"246","Abu Nadrah says that I said to Abu Sa'id (Khudri) رضي الله عنه that indeed you narrate to us very beloved hadith from the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم, so if we write them down? He said: Write it, and I will never make it the Qur'an."
"247","Sayyiduna Mahmood bin Rabee’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from ‘Itbaan bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he related to him a hadith about Ibn Dukhayshum (may Allah be pleased with him). Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I came to Madinah and met ‘Itbaan (may Allah be pleased with him), and he narrated that hadith to me. Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I liked that hadith very much, so I told my son to write it down, and he wrote it."
"248","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed a man came to him and asked him about something. He narrated a hadith to him. The man said: Narrate to me from the Book of Allah and do not narrate from anything else. So he said: Indeed, you are a foolish man. Do you find in the Qur'an that the Zuhr prayer is four rak'ahs, and that it is not to be recited aloud, and the number of prayers and the amount of zakat, etc.? Then he said: Do you find this in detail in the Book of Allah? Indeed, the Book of Allah has certainly stated this in a decisive manner, and the Sunnah explains it."
"249","Sahl bin Abi Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif said that my father said to Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): O uncle! Surely the people are no longer those people among whom you used to spend your time; now they are merely wolves in clothing, so beware of them. He replied: Listen, by Allah! Indeed, if you have said this, then certainly, in a short while, I have been put in doubt by them to the extent that I narrate a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and they say: Did you hear it with your own ears?"
"250","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps his tongue straight with the truth, and then acts upon it, his reward continues for the Day of Resurrection, then on the Day of Resurrection Allah will grant him his full reward."""
"251","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among us just as I am standing among you, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “By Him besides Whom there is no deity worthy of worship! The blood of a man who testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful, except in one of three cases: a life for a life, a married adulterer, and the one who separates from the community, abandoning his religion—or he said: leaving Islam.”"
"252","Sayyiduna Sanabhi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""I will precede you at the Hawd (the Pond), and indeed I will boast of your multitude before the other nations. So do not fight one another after me at all."""
"253","Abdur Rahman bin Aaidh narrates that indeed Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Masjid Al-Aqsa and prayed in it. He met some people there, and they began to walk with him. They asked, ""How did you come?"" He replied that his companionship was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). ""We have come so that we may greet you and listen to you."" He said, ""Dismount and pray."" Then he said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Whoever dies and does not associate anything with Allah and does not shed any of the forbidden blood, he will enter Paradise through whichever of its doors he wishes.'"""
"254","Abu Nadrah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that the one who was present at the sermon of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in Mina related this hadith to me. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood during the days of Tashreeq and said: ""O people! Indeed, your Lord is one and indeed, your father is one. Listen! There is no superiority of an Arab over a non-Arab, nor of a non-Arab over an Arab, nor of a black over a red, nor of a red over a black, except by the piety of Allah. Behold! Have I conveyed (the message)?"" They said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has conveyed (the message). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is necessary that those who are present convey it to those who are absent."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What month is this?"" They said: It is the sacred month. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What day is this?"" They said: It is the sacred day. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What city is this?"" They said: It is the sacred city. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, your blood and your wealth (the narrator said: and I think he said: and your honor) are sacred for you, just as the sanctity of this city, in this month, on this day of yours. Behold! Have I conveyed (the message)?"" They said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has conveyed (the message). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""So it is necessary that those who are present convey it to those who are not present."""
"255","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah. So when they say that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah, and they face our Qiblah, and eat our slaughtered animals, and perform our prayer, then indeed their blood and wealth become forbidden for us, except by right. For them are the rights that are for the Muslims, and upon them are the obligations that are upon (the rest of) the Muslims."""
"256","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon at Jabiyah (a place) and said: Among us, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up just as I am standing among you, and he (peace be upon him) said: “Accept my advice of goodness regarding my Companions (may Allah be pleased with them), then regarding those who will come after them, then regarding those who will come after them. Then falsehood will become widespread, to the extent that a man will begin to give testimony before he is asked for it, and will begin to swear an oath before it is demanded from him. Whoever among you desires the middle of Paradise, let him adhere to the congregation, for indeed, Satan is with the one who is alone, and he is farther from two. And none of you is ever alone with a woman except that Satan is the third among them. And whoever is pleased by his good deed and displeased by his sin, then he is a believer.”"
"257","It is narrated from Sayyida Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her), she said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will be rulers over you who will recognize their own rights but deny your rights. Whoever rejects them has certainly attained salvation, and whoever dislikes them is indeed safe, but whoever is pleased with them and follows them..."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Should we not fight them? He said: ""No, as long as they establish the prayer."""
"258","Sayyiduna Awf bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The best of your rulers are those whom you love and they love you, and you pray for them and they pray for you. And the worst of your rulers are those whom you hate and they hate you, you curse them and they curse you."" He said: We said, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Should we not declare war against them at that time? He said: ""No, as long as they establish the prayer. But if a person has a ruler appointed over him and he sees him committing something of disobedience to Allah, then he should dislike that act of disobedience to Allah which he commits, but he should not withdraw his hand from obedience."""
"259","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Mas'ud) رضي الله عنه, who reports from the Prophet Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم that he said: ""Indeed, the matter is that soon there will be selfishness, tribulations, and such affairs which you will disapprove of."" They said, ""O Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم! What do you command for the one who encounters this?"" He صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""Fulfill the rights that are upon you, and ask Allah for your own rights."""
"260","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: ""O Abu Dharr! What will you do when people will be hungry, to the extent that you will not have the strength to stand from your bed to your mosque and from your mosque to your bed?"" I said, Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) know best. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adopt chastity."" Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What will you do when people die, to the extent that a house will be with a servant?"" I said, Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) know best. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be patient."" Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How will you act when people fight among themselves until even the den of a wolf is recognized?"" I said, Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) know best. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then go to where you belong."" I said, What is your opinion if I am approached? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Enter your house."" I said, What is your opinion if I am still approached? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you fear that the flash of the sword will overcome you, then place the edge of your garment over your face; he will return with your sin and his own sin."" I said, Should I not take up arms? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then you will become his partner."""
"261","Muhammad bin Abdul Malik narrated that indeed Mughira bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) entered upon Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was at the door, and (the rebels) had besieged him. So (Mughira, may Allah be pleased with him) said: Choose one of three things: either we burn another door for you besides the one upon which they (the rebels) are, so you can go out, then mount your ride and go to Makkah; they will never feel at ease with you while you are there. Or you mount your ride and go to Sham (Syria). Indeed, they are the people of Sham and among them is Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him). Or you take those who are with you and go out; surely you have a large number and strength with you, you fight, you are upon the truth and they are upon falsehood. Upon this, Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) said: As for your suggestion that I mount my ride until I reach Makkah, indeed, they will never feel at ease with me while I am there. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “A man from Quraysh will commit heresy in Makkah, upon him will be poured the punishment of the worlds,” so I will never be that man. As for your suggestion that I mount my ride and go to Sham, indeed, they are the people of Sham and among them is Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him), but I will never leave my place of migration and the neighborhood of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in it. And as for your suggestion that I take those who are with me and go out, I will never be the first to oppose the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) by filling a vial with unjustly shed blood."
"262","Abu Burdah bin Abi Musa narrates that we passed by ""Rabadha"" when suddenly there was a tent and a pavilion. We asked, ""Whose is this?"" It was said that it belongs to Muhammad bin Maslamah (may Allah be pleased with him). I entered upon him and said: May Allah have mercy on you. Why do you not go out to the people? Surely, you are in such a position in this matter that your word would be listened to. He replied that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the matter is that soon there will be tribulation and division, so strike your sword on the width of Uhud, break your arrows, cut your bowstring, and sit in your house."" He said: I did exactly what the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded me, and suddenly a sword was tied to the pillar of the tent. He drew it, and unexpectedly it was a wooden sword. Then he said: Indeed, I have done with my sword exactly what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded me, and I have prepared it; with it, I frighten the people."
"263","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with both of them), he says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, before the Day of Resurrection there will be such tribulations as if they are pieces of a dark night. A man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and in the evening he will be a believer and in the morning a disbeliever. People will sell their share (of religion) for a small portion of worldly goods, or (he said) for worldly goods."""
"264","Hasan said: By Allah, besides whom there is no deity worthy of worship, we have seen them: they have forms but no intellect, bodies but no understanding or awareness. They are like moths of the fire, flies of greed and desire. In the morning they go out with two dirhams and return with two dirhams. One of them sells his religion for the price of a goat."
"265","Lady Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that indeed one day she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying from the pulpit: ""O people!"" She said that at that time she was having her hair combed, so she said to the woman who was combing her hair, ""Woe to you, leave my head."" The woman said, ""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) is merely calling the people."" She replied, ""Are we not among the people?"" So she wrapped her head and stood behind her chamber and heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""O people! Indeed, I will be at the Hawd (the Pond) during that time, when you will be passed in groups, and you will be taken on different paths. I will call you, 'Listen! Come to this path.' Then a caller will call out from behind me, 'Indeed, they changed (the religion) after you.' I will say: 'Beware! Distance, distance.'"""
"266","Muhammad bin Abi Abdur Rahman bin Labeebah narrated that indeed Umar bin Sa’d went to his father (Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him), who was at Aqeeq on his separate land, and said: O my father! Among the companions of Badr and the people of Shura, none remain except you (may Allah be pleased with you). If indeed you raise yourself and stand up for the people, not even two men will disagree with you. He replied: O my son! I will answer this. I remained seated until my life is left as much as the quick passing of a beast, then I should go out and cause some of the Ummah of Muhammad (peace be upon him) to fight others? Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: “Surely the best provision is that which suffices, and the best remembrance is that which is hidden.”"
"267","Qais bin Abad narrated that we said to Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him): What is your opinion about your fighting— is it an opinion that you have formed, for indeed an opinion can be wrong or right, or is it a covenant that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made with you? He replied: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not make any such covenant with us that he did not make with all the other people."
"268","Qais bin Abad said that we were with Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). Whenever he attended a gathering place, or climbed a hill, or descended into a valley, he would affirm Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him). I said to a man from Banu Yashkur, ""Come with us to the Commander of the Faithful, so that we may ask him about his statement, 'Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) have spoken the truth.'"" So we went to him and said, ""O Commander of the Faithful! We have seen that whenever you attend a gathering place or climb a hill, you say: 'Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) have spoken the truth.' Has the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made any covenant with you regarding this?"" He turned away, but when we insisted, he said: ""By Allah! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not make any covenant with me, except for what he took from the people. But the people attacked Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) and martyred him, and besides me, regarding this (caliphate), there was no one in a worse state or with worse deeds than me. I thought that indeed I was more entitled to it than them, so I assumed it. Allah knows best whether we were right or mistaken."""
"269","Qutbah bin Malik said that Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Who is Ali bin Abi Talib? So Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: Listen! Surely you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has forbidden speaking ill of the deceased, so why are you speaking ill of Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), when he has passed away?"
"270","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that when Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was placed on his bier before burial, people gathered around him and began to pray for him. I was among them. Only one person made me anxious, who held my shoulder from behind. I turned and saw that it was Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him). He prayed for mercy for Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: ""You have not left behind anyone whose deeds I would prefer to meet Allah with, more than yours. By Allah! I am certain that Allah will join you with your two companions (the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him), and the reason is that I have often heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'I went, and Abu Bakr and Umar went; I entered, and Abu Bakr and Umar entered; I came out, and Abu Bakr and Umar came out.' So I am sure that Allah will certainly join you with both of them."""
"271","Abu Imran Jouni (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I said to Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him): I have pledged allegiance to Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both) on the condition that I will fight against the people of Sham. He said: Perhaps you want to go around saying: Jundub told me this, Jundub told me that. I said: No, I am only asking you for a fatwa, please do give me a fatwa. He said: Pay ransom for yourself with your wealth. I said: That will not be accepted from me. Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Indeed, during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I was a strong young man, and so-and-so (Companion) told me that indeed he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the slain will come clinging to the killer and will say: O Lord! He killed me. Allah will say to him: For what reason did you kill him? He will say: For the kingdom of so-and-so. Therefore, I want you not to be that person."""
"272","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is only destruction in the killing of a Muslim,"" and he said this three times."
"273","And Ibn Hanifah, may Allah have mercy on him, said: If indeed all the people give me allegiance, except for one man, and my authority would not be established without him, then I would not accept this (allegiance)."
"274","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: While we were around the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), suddenly he mentioned tribulations, or it was mentioned to him, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you see that people's covenants have become corrupted and their trusts have become light, and they have become like this."" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interlaced his fingers. So I stood up towards the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! What should I do at that time? May Allah ransom me for you. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Adhere to your house, restrain your tongue, take hold of what you recognize, and leave what you deny. Make your own self your special concern, and leave the general public to their own affairs."""
"275","Haroon bin Saad narrated that Haneef bin Sajq encountered the army of Ibn Diljah from the people of Shaam at the place of Rabdhah, fought them, and defeated them. Then Haneef entered Madinah and met Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and said: O Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)! What is it that keeps you behind from Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both)? Are you not his brother from old times? Surely, people are staying behind from him because of your delay. So he said: Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him), and indeed he put his hand in his mouth and said, Do you know what it means to put the hand in the mouth? He said: No. He said: Have you not seen a woman who breastfeeds her child, until when he is satisfied or full, he becomes uninterested and puts his hand in his mouth, so his mother says: He has put his hand in his mouth. And indeed, by Allah! I will surely become like a heavy-weighted camel. And do you know what a heavy-weighted camel is? He said: No. He said: It is the camel that separates itself and sits down and always remains in its sitting place until it is slaughtered there. So I am like that camel. I will confine myself to my house until there comes to me the one who slaughters me in it, or the people gather upon one man. If they gather upon a righteous group among themselves (then it is correct), and if they become divided and scattered, then I will not gather with them in their division, nor will I act (give allegiance) to two men, after I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever is entrusted by Allah with the responsibility of any subjects, on the Day of Resurrection he will surely be questioned about them: did he establish Allah’s command among them or did he neglect it, until a man will be questioned about his household: did he establish Allah’s command among them or did he neglect it.”"
"276","Rabi’ bin Hirash narrates that I heard a man at the funeral of Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: I heard the one on the bier saying, “I have no objection, ever since I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: However, if you fight, I will surely enter my house, and if anyone enters upon me, I will surely say: Come and bear my sin along with your own sin.”"
"277","Usayd bin Mutashams bin Muawiyah narrates that we fought the battle of Isfahan with Abu Musa (Ash’ari) (may Allah be pleased with him). Shortly after, he conquered it, then after some time he returned and we also returned with him. We camped at a place and Aqil was a neighbor there. (Abu Musa Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Who will take down his pillow?” So I stood up towards him and took it down. He said, “Shall I not narrate to you the hadith which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to narrate to us?” We said, “Why not, may Allah have mercy on you.” He said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) told us: ‘Indeed, before the Day of Judgment there will be ‘Harj’.’ We asked, ‘What is ‘Harj’?’ He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘Killing and bloodshed.’ We said, ‘Every year most of the disbelievers are killed. Indeed, in a year we kill so many disbelievers.’ He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘No, by Allah! Your killing of the disbelievers is not that ‘Harj’, rather it is the killing which will be reconciliation (meaning among the people of Islam), O group of Muslims! Until a man will kill his neighbor, his cousin, his brother, and his father.’ He said, ‘We were astonished and dumbfounded, so much so that no one was even opening his eyes. Some of us looked at others and we said: How will a man kill his brother, his cousin, and his father, because of the love and affection which Allah has placed in our hearts on that day? And we know that our companion has not lied to us.’ We said, ‘What do you think, will the intellects we have today be with us on that day?’ He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘No, by Allah! (Satan) will cause discord in their intellects just as he will in the people of that time, and the people will be responsible for that. We will think that indeed they are upon something, but they will not be upon anything.’ And by Allah! Indeed, I fear that (time) will reach me and especially you, and by Allah! If that (time) reaches me and especially you, I will not find any way out for myself and for you, in that matter regarding which our Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took a covenant from us. Yes, one can come out of it in the same way as he entered it.” Hasan said: That is, in a state of reconciliation."
"278","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The time is near when the best wealth of a Muslim will be sheep, which he will follow to the tops of mountains and places where rain falls, fleeing with his religion from tribulations."""
"279","Wabisa Asadi narrated that indeed I was inside my house in Kufa when I heard: ""Peace be upon you (may I enter?)"" I said, ""And peace be upon you (please enter)."" When he came in, suddenly it was Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him). I said, ""O Abu Abdur Rahman! What is this time for a meeting?"" And it was midday. He said, ""The day became long for me, and I thought about whom I could talk to."" He said that he began to narrate to me the hadiths of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and I began to narrate them to him. Then he started narrating a hadith to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""There will be a tribulation; the one who is sleeping during it is better than the one lying down, the one lying down is better than the one sitting, the one sitting is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, the one walking is better than the one riding, and the one riding is better than the one running. All those killed in it will be in the Fire."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! And when will that be?"" He said: ""It will be during the days of 'Harj' (killing)."" He said, ""I asked, and when will the days of 'Harj' be?"" He said: ""When a man will not be safe from his companion."" He said, ""I asked: If I reach that time, what do you command me to do?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Restrain your life and your hands, and enter your neighborhood."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What do you think, if he enters upon me in my neighborhood?"" He said, ""What do you think, if he enters upon me in my house?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Enter your mosque, and do likewise."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) clasped his right hand on his wrist and said: ""My Lord is Allah alone, until you are killed upon that."""
"280","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hayan narrated that indeed a man narrated to him from his father Yahya that he was with Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), so Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said to him: ""You do not consider killing during tribulation to be anything, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has said: 'Two people should not whisper together excluding a third.'"""
"281","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent an army and appointed a man as their leader. He lit a fire and said: Enter into it. Some people intended to enter it, while others said: It is from this (fire) that we have fled. This matter was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so regarding those who intended to enter it, he said: ""If you had entered it, you would have remained in it until the Day of Resurrection."" And for the others, he said a good word or said: ""You did well, there is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah; obedience is only in goodness."""
"282","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Soon there will be rulers who will be surrounded by courtiers and friends from among the people; they will commit oppression and speak lies. Whoever helps them in their oppression and affirms them as truthful despite their lies, then he is not from me and I am not from him. And whoever does not affirm them in their lies and does not help them in their oppression, then he is from me and I am from him."""
"283","Hasan narrates that Ma'qil bin Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) fell ill with the illness in which he passed away. When his condition became heavy, Ibn Ziyad came to his house to visit him. When he sat beside him, Ma'qil (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Indeed, I am going to narrate to you a hadith which I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever is made a guardian over a people and does not surround them with goodwill, then surely Allah has made the fragrance of Paradise forbidden for him, and its fragrance is found at a distance of a hundred years’ journey."" Ibn Ziyad said: Why did you not narrate this hadith before today? He said: Even today, if it were not for the condition I am in, I would not have narrated it to you."
"284","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the most beloved of people to Allah and the closest to me in assembly among them will be the just ruler, and on the Day of Resurrection, the most disliked of people to Allah and the one with the severest punishment among them will be the oppressive ruler."""
"285","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he reports from the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Soon you will covet leadership, and indeed it will be a cause of regret and sorrow on the Day of Resurrection. Good is the one who nurses, and bad is the one who weans."""
"286","Jahm bin Aws narrated that I heard Abdullah bin Abi Maryam, and Ubaidullah bin Rustam passed by him on his mount. He said to Ibn Abi Maryam, ""Indeed, I desire your company and to converse with you."" When he left, Ibn Abi Maryam said: I heard Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Never envy a wicked person because of his blessings, for you do not know what he will encounter after his death. Surely, for him with Allah is such a killer that never dies."" This hadith reached Wahb bin Munabbih, so Wahb sent Abu Dawood A'war to him and said: ""O so-and-so, who is that killer who never dies?"" Ibn Abi Maryam said: ""Death."""
"287","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those who show mercy, the Most Merciful will show mercy to them. Show mercy to those on the earth, the One in the heavens will show mercy to you."""
"288","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she reports from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever is gentle with my Ummah, Allah will be gentle with him, and whoever is harsh upon my Ummah, Allah will be harsh upon him."""
"289","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever is a ruler or leader, he will certainly have two confidants: one confidant who commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and (the other) confidant who does not refrain from causing him any harm. Whoever is protected from his evil, indeed he is protected, and he is the one who prevails over both of them."""
